window.REV_FLIP=window.REV_FLIP||{};window.REV_FLIP["terraform"]=[{"id":"terraform-f0001","card":"q-terraform-001-terraform-and-infrastructure-as-code","sec":"terraform-s002","q":"What is Terraform, and how does it differ from Ansible or CloudFormation?","a":"<p>Terraform is a declarative IaC tool that provisions infrastructure across clouds. Ansible is procedural and excels at configuration management. CloudFormation is AWS-only and uses JSON/YAML, which is less readable than Terraform's HCL.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"terraform-f0002","card":"q-terraform-001-terraform-and-infrastructure-as-code","sec":"terraform-s002","q":"What is Infrastructure as Code (IaC), and why is it important?","a":"<p>IaC is managing and provisioning infrastructure through machine-readable definition files instead of manual processes. It gives consistency, scalability, automation and version control. Terraform is declarative, uses HCL, supports many cloud providers and keeps a state file so operations are idempotent. Ansible is procedural, uses YAML playbooks, is agentless (SSH) and excels at configuration management and application deployment. Terraform focuses on provisioning, Ansible on configuration.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"terraform-f0003","card":"q-terraform-001-terraform-and-infrastructure-as-code","sec":"terraform-s002","q":"What are the key components of Terraform?","a":"<ul>\n  <li><strong>Providers</strong>: bridges to cloud APIs.</li>\n  <li><strong>Resources</strong>: the infrastructure pieces.</li>\n  <li><strong>Modules</strong>: reusable configs.</li>\n  <li><strong>State</strong>: tracks reality.</li>\n  <li><strong>Variables</strong>: inputs.</li>\n  <li><strong>Outputs</strong>: results.</li>\n</ul>","hand":false},{"id":"terraform-f0004","card":"q-terraform-002-init-plan-apply-and-destroy","sec":"terraform-s003","q":"What is the purpose of <code>terraform init</code>?","a":"<p>It sets up the project: downloads providers, configures the backend and fetches modules.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>terraform init</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"terraform-f0005","card":"q-terraform-002-init-plan-apply-and-destroy","sec":"terraform-s003","q":"What does <code>terraform plan</code> do, and why is it useful?","a":"<p>It shows what will change by comparing desired and current state. It catches errors early and lets you review safely.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>terraform plan</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"terraform-f0006","card":"q-terraform-002-init-plan-apply-and-destroy","sec":"terraform-s003","q":"How does <code>terraform apply</code> work?","a":"<p>It executes the plan: creates, updates or deletes resources and updates state. It prompts for confirmation unless <code>-auto-approve</code> is used.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>terraform apply</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"terraform-f0007","card":"q-terraform-002-init-plan-apply-and-destroy","sec":"terraform-s003","q":"What is the purpose of <code>terraform destroy</code>?","a":"<p>It deletes all managed resources, a cleanup tool.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>terraform destroy</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"terraform-f0008","card":"q-terraform-003-state-file-and-providers","sec":"terraform-s004","q":"What is the Terraform state file, and why is it critical?","a":"<p>It maps configuration to real infrastructure. If it is lost, Terraform is blind and you get duplicates or errors.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"terraform-f0009","card":"q-terraform-003-state-file-and-providers","sec":"terraform-s004","q":"What is a Terraform provider, and how do you configure one?","a":"<p>A provider is the API bridge to clouds and services. Define it like this:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>provider &quot;aws&quot; {\n    region = &quot;us-east-1&quot;\n}</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"terraform-f0010","card":"q-terraform-004-variables-backends-and-hcl","sec":"terraform-s005","q":"What is the difference between <code>terraform.tfvars</code> and <code>variables.tf</code>?","a":"<p><code>variables.tf</code> declares variables (type, default). <code>terraform.tfvars</code> sets their values.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"terraform-f0011","card":"q-terraform-004-variables-backends-and-hcl","sec":"terraform-s005","q":"How do you define variables and assign values in Terraform?","a":"<p>Define:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>variable &quot;size&quot; { \n    type = string \n    default = &quot;t2.micro&quot; \n}</code></pre></div>\n<p>Assign through the default, a tfvars file, <code>-var</code>, <code>TF_VAR_</code> environment variables, or the interactive prompt.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"terraform-f0012","card":"q-terraform-004-variables-backends-and-hcl","sec":"terraform-s005","q":"Which backends does Terraform support, and why use a remote one?","a":"<p>Local, S3, Terraform Cloud and others. A remote backend gives team access, locking and durability.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"terraform-f0013","card":"q-terraform-004-variables-backends-and-hcl","sec":"terraform-s005","q":"What is HCL, and how does it compare to JSON in Terraform?","a":"<p>HCL is a readable, comment-friendly config language. JSON is verbose and machine-oriented. Both work, but HCL is human-first.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"terraform-f0014","card":"q-terraform-005-installing-terraform-and-data-sources","sec":"terraform-s006","q":"How do you install Terraform, and what is needed?","a":"<p>Download the binary, add it to PATH and verify. You need an OS, internet access and optionally Git.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>terraform -version</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"terraform-f0015","card":"q-terraform-005-installing-terraform-and-data-sources","sec":"terraform-s006","q":"What is the difference between a resource and a data source?","a":"<p>A resource is managed infrastructure (Terraform creates and deletes it). A data source is a read-only lookup of something that already exists.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"terraform-f0016","card":"q-terraform-006-standard-workflow-and-plan","sec":"terraform-s007","q":"What is the typical Terraform workflow?","a":"<p><code>init</code> (setup), <code>plan</code> (preview), <code>apply</code> (execute), <code>destroy</code> (teardown).</p>","hand":false},{"id":"terraform-f0017","card":"q-terraform-006-standard-workflow-and-plan","sec":"terraform-s007","q":"What happens if you apply without a plan?","a":"<p>Terraform plans and applies automatically. This is risky because there is no preview.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"terraform-f0018","card":"q-terraform-006-standard-workflow-and-plan","sec":"terraform-s007","q":"How do you preview changes without applying?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>terraform plan</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"terraform-f0019","card":"q-terraform-007-refresh-validate-and-format","sec":"terraform-s008","q":"What does <code>terraform refresh</code> do?","a":"<p>It syncs state with real infrastructure without changing any resource.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"terraform-f0020","card":"q-terraform-007-refresh-validate-and-format","sec":"terraform-s008","q":"How do you validate a Terraform configuration?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>terraform validate</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"terraform-f0021","card":"q-terraform-007-refresh-validate-and-format","sec":"terraform-s008","q":"What is the purpose of <code>terraform fmt</code>?","a":"<p>It formats code consistently.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>terraform fmt</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"terraform-f0022","card":"q-terraform-008-import-taint-and-output","sec":"terraform-s009","q":"How do you import existing infrastructure into Terraform?","a":"<p>Define the resource block, then import it.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>terraform import aws_instance.example i-1234567890abcdef0</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"terraform-f0023","card":"q-terraform-008-import-taint-and-output","sec":"terraform-s009","q":"What is <code>terraform taint</code>, and when do you use it?","a":"<p>It marks a resource for recreation on the next apply. Use it for corrupted or stuck resources.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>terraform taint aws_instance.example</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"terraform-f0024","card":"q-terraform-008-import-taint-and-output","sec":"terraform-s009","q":"How do you roll back changes if something fails?","a":"<p>Revert the configuration and apply again. There is no automatic rollback, so rely on Git and backups.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"terraform-f0025","card":"q-terraform-008-import-taint-and-output","sec":"terraform-s009","q":"What does <code>terraform output</code> do?","a":"<p>It shows output values after apply.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>terraform output</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"terraform-f0026","card":"q-terraform-009-defining-variables","sec":"terraform-s010","q":"How do you define a variable with a default?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>variable &quot;region&quot; { \n    type = string \n    default = &quot;us-east-1&quot; \n}</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"terraform-f0027","card":"q-terraform-009-defining-variables","sec":"terraform-s010","q":"Which variable types does Terraform have?","a":"<p>String, number, bool, list, map, set, object, tuple.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"terraform-f0028","card":"q-terraform-009-defining-variables","sec":"terraform-s010","q":"How do you pass variables on the command line?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>terraform apply -var=&quot;size=t3.large&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"terraform-f0029","card":"q-terraform-009-defining-variables","sec":"terraform-s010","q":"What is the difference between input and local variables?","a":"<p>Input variables (<code>variable</code>) are external and customizable. Local values (<code>locals</code>) are internal and computed.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"terraform-f0030","card":"q-terraform-009-defining-variables","sec":"terraform-s010","q":"How do you reference an output from another module?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>vpc_id = module.vpc.vpc_id</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"terraform-f0031","card":"q-terraform-010-sensitive-values","sec":"terraform-s011","q":"How do you secure sensitive variables?","a":"<p>Use tfvars files that are gitignored, environment variables (<code>TF_VAR_</code>), or Vault/Secrets Manager.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"terraform-f0032","card":"q-terraform-010-sensitive-values","sec":"terraform-s011","q":"What is the <code>sensitive</code> attribute?","a":"<p>It hides a variable or output in logs. Use it for secrets.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>output &quot;pass&quot; { \n    value = &quot;secret&quot; \n    sensitive = true \n}</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"terraform-f0033","card":"q-terraform-011-count-for-each-and-conditionals","sec":"terraform-s012","q":"How do you use <code>count</code> with resources?","a":"<p>It multiplies the resource.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>resource &quot;aws_instance&quot; &quot;server&quot; { \n    count = 2 \n}</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"terraform-f0034","card":"q-terraform-011-count-for-each-and-conditionals","sec":"terraform-s012","q":"What is <code>for_each</code>, and how does it differ from <code>count</code>?","a":"<p><code>for_each</code> iterates over a map or set with keys. <code>count</code> gives only a numeric index.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>for_each = { &quot;a&quot; = &quot;val1&quot;, &quot;b&quot; = &quot;val2&quot; }</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"terraform-f0035","card":"q-terraform-011-count-for-each-and-conditionals","sec":"terraform-s012","q":"How do you conditionally create resources?","a":"<p>Use <code>count</code> with a condition.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>count = var.create ? 1 : 0</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"terraform-f0036","card":"q-terraform-012-module-basics","sec":"terraform-s013","q":"What is a Terraform module?","a":"<p>A reusable bundle of configuration that simplifies and standardizes infrastructure.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"terraform-f0037","card":"q-terraform-012-module-basics","sec":"terraform-s013","q":"How do you create a reusable module?","a":"<p>Make a directory with <code>main.tf</code>, <code>variables.tf</code> and <code>outputs.tf</code>, and parameterize it.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"terraform-f0038","card":"q-terraform-012-module-basics","sec":"terraform-s013","q":"What is the difference between a root and a child module?","a":"<p>The root module is the main directory where commands run. A child module is a called submodule that can be reused.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"terraform-f0039","card":"q-terraform-012-module-basics","sec":"terraform-s013","q":"How do you pass variables to a module?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>module &quot;vpc&quot; { \n    source = &quot;./vpc&quot; \n    cidr = &quot;10.0.0.0/16&quot; \n}</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"terraform-f0040","card":"q-terraform-013-sources-versions-and-the-registry","sec":"terraform-s014","q":"What are module sources?","a":"<p>Local paths (<code>./</code>), Git, or the Registry. A remote source:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>source = &quot;terraform-aws-modules/vpc/aws&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"terraform-f0041","card":"q-terraform-013-sources-versions-and-the-registry","sec":"terraform-s014","q":"How do you version Terraform modules?","a":"<p>Use Git tags (<code>v1.0.0</code>) or the Registry <code>version = \"2.0\"</code> argument.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"terraform-f0042","card":"q-terraform-013-sources-versions-and-the-registry","sec":"terraform-s014","q":"What is the Terraform Module Registry?","a":"<p>HashiCorp's module hub.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>module &quot;s3&quot; { \n    source = &quot;terraform-aws-modules/s3-bucket/aws&quot; \n}</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"terraform-f0043","card":"q-terraform-014-debugging-and-nesting-modules","sec":"terraform-s015","q":"How do you debug module issues?","a":"<p>Use logs (<code>TF_LOG=DEBUG</code>), <code>plan</code>, and temporary outputs.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"terraform-f0044","card":"q-terraform-014-debugging-and-nesting-modules","sec":"terraform-s015","q":"Can you nest modules, and is there a depth limit?","a":"<p>Yes, modules can call modules. There is no hard limit, but keep nesting shallow (2-3 levels).</p>","hand":false},{"id":"terraform-f0045","card":"q-terraform-014-debugging-and-nesting-modules","sec":"terraform-s015","q":"How do you update a module without breaking infrastructure?","a":"<p>Test the new version, pin it, and check the plan for no recreation.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"terraform-f0046","card":"q-terraform-015-why-state-matters","sec":"terraform-s016","q":"Why is the state file key, and what if it is corrupted?","a":"<p>It tracks infrastructure. Corruption causes duplicates and errors. Restore from backup.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"terraform-f0047","card":"q-terraform-015-why-state-matters","sec":"terraform-s016","q":"How do you recover a lost state file?","a":"<p>Restore a backup or rebuild it with <code>terraform import</code>.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"terraform-f0048","card":"q-terraform-015-why-state-matters","sec":"terraform-s016","q":"What is state drift, and how do you fix it?","a":"<p>Drift is a mismatch between real infrastructure and state. Detect it with <code>plan</code>. Fix it with <code>apply</code> or by updating the config.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"terraform-f0049","card":"q-terraform-016-remote-backends-and-locking","sec":"terraform-s017","q":"How do you configure a remote backend (S3, Terraform Cloud)?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>terraform { \n    backend &quot;s3&quot; { \n        bucket = &quot;state&quot; \n        key = &quot;tfstate&quot; \n    } \n}</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"terraform-f0050","card":"q-terraform-016-remote-backends-and-locking","sec":"terraform-s017","q":"What are the benefits of remote state?","a":"<p>Collaboration, locking, safety and versioning.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"terraform-f0051","card":"q-terraform-016-remote-backends-and-locking","sec":"terraform-s017","q":"Can you lock the state file, and why?","a":"<p>Locking is automatic with remote backends (for example DynamoDB with S3). It prevents race conditions.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"terraform-f0052","card":"q-terraform-016-remote-backends-and-locking","sec":"terraform-s017","q":"How do you share state across a team?","a":"<p>Use a remote backend with access control and locking.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"terraform-f0053","card":"q-terraform-016-remote-backends-and-locking","sec":"terraform-s017","q":"What happens with two simultaneous <code>terraform apply</code> runs?","a":"<p>With local state they overwrite each other, which is chaos. With a remote backend and locking, one run fails.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"terraform-f0054","card":"q-terraform-017-state-commands","sec":"terraform-s018","q":"How do you move a resource between state files?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>terraform state mv -state-out=../new.tfstate aws_instance.example aws_instance.example</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"terraform-f0055","card":"q-terraform-017-state-commands","sec":"terraform-s018","q":"What is <code>terraform state</code>, and what are its subcommands?","a":"<p>It manages state: <code>mv</code> (move), <code>rm</code> (remove), <code>list</code>, <code>show</code>.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"terraform-f0056","card":"q-terraform-018-multiple-providers-and-aliases","sec":"terraform-s019","q":"How do you configure multiple providers?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>provider &quot;aws&quot; { \n    region = &quot;us-east-1&quot; \n}\nprovider &quot;aws&quot; { \n    alias = &quot;west&quot; \n    region = &quot;us-west-2&quot; \n}</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"terraform-f0057","card":"q-terraform-018-multiple-providers-and-aliases","sec":"terraform-s019","q":"What is provider aliasing?","a":"<p>It names provider variants, for example for multiple regions.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>resource &quot;aws_instance&quot; &quot;west&quot; { \n    provider = aws.west \n}</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"terraform-f0058","card":"q-terraform-019-versions-and-authentication","sec":"terraform-s020","q":"How do you specify a provider version?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>terraform { \n    required_providers { \n        aws = { version = &quot;~&gt; 4.0&quot; } \n    } \n}</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"terraform-f0059","card":"q-terraform-019-versions-and-authentication","sec":"terraform-s020","q":"What happens if you do not specify a provider version?","a":"<p>Terraform grabs the latest, which risks inconsistency and breakage.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"terraform-f0060","card":"q-terraform-019-versions-and-authentication","sec":"terraform-s020","q":"How do you authenticate with AWS, Azure and GCP?","a":"<ul>\n  <li><strong>AWS</strong>: environment variables (<code>AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID</code>).</li>\n  <li><strong>Azure</strong>: CLI login (<code>az login</code>).</li>\n  <li><strong>GCP</strong>: key file (<code>GOOGLE_CREDENTIALS</code>).</li>\n</ul>","hand":false},{"id":"terraform-f0061","card":"q-terraform-019-versions-and-authentication","sec":"terraform-s020","q":"What is the difference between an official and a community provider?","a":"<p>Official providers are HashiCorp-backed and stable. Community providers are third-party with variable quality.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"terraform-f0062","card":"q-terraform-019-versions-and-authentication","sec":"terraform-s020","q":"How do you troubleshoot provider errors?","a":"<p>Check logs (<code>TF_LOG</code>), credentials, configuration and versions.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"terraform-f0063","card":"q-terraform-020-organizing-code-and-files","sec":"terraform-s021","q":"How do you organize Terraform code for big projects?","a":"<p>Use modules, naming conventions, environment directories, remote state and DRY principles.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"terraform-f0064","card":"q-terraform-020-organizing-code-and-files","sec":"terraform-s021","q":"How do you structure Terraform files?","a":"<p><code>main.tf</code>, <code>variables.tf</code>, <code>outputs.tf</code>, <code>providers.tf</code>, <code>locals.tf</code>.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"terraform-f0065","card":"q-terraform-020-organizing-code-and-files","sec":"terraform-s021","q":"How do you avoid hardcoding?","a":"<p>Use variables, data sources, locals and modules.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"terraform-f0066","card":"q-terraform-021-secrets-and-teamwork","sec":"terraform-s022","q":"How do you handle secrets?","a":"<p>Use <code>sensitive</code> variables, Vault, or environment variables, never hardcoded values.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"terraform-f0067","card":"q-terraform-021-secrets-and-teamwork","sec":"terraform-s022","q":"How do you manage Terraform in teams?","a":"<p>Remote state, workspaces, Git and CI/CD.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"terraform-f0068","card":"q-terraform-021-secrets-and-teamwork","sec":"terraform-s022","q":"What is the role of version control?","a":"<p>It tracks changes, enables collaboration and makes code reproducible.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"terraform-f0069","card":"q-terraform-022-idempotency-dependencies-and-pitfalls","sec":"terraform-s023","q":"How do you ensure idempotency?","a":"<p>Stay declarative, avoid provisioners and use unique IDs.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"terraform-f0070","card":"q-terraform-022-idempotency-dependencies-and-pitfalls","sec":"terraform-s023","q":"How do you handle resource dependencies?","a":"<p>Implicit dependencies come from references. Explicit ones use <code>depends_on</code>.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"terraform-f0071","card":"q-terraform-022-idempotency-dependencies-and-pitfalls","sec":"terraform-s023","q":"What are common Terraform pitfalls?","a":"<p>Hardcoding secrets, manual changes, skipping <code>plan</code>, and version mismatches.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"terraform-f0072","card":"q-terraform-023-workspaces-and-environments","sec":"terraform-s024","q":"What is a Terraform workspace?","a":"<p>Multiple states in one directory.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>terraform workspace new dev</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"terraform-f0073","card":"q-terraform-023-workspaces-and-environments","sec":"terraform-s024","q":"How do you manage multiple environments (dev, prod)?","a":"<p>Use workspaces, separate directories, or variables (<code>-var env=prod</code>).</p>","hand":false},{"id":"terraform-f0074","card":"q-terraform-024-depends-on-and-dynamic-blocks","sec":"terraform-s025","q":"What is <code>depends_on</code>?","a":"<p>It forces ordering when implicit dependencies are not enough.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>depends_on = [aws_vpc.main]</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"terraform-f0075","card":"q-terraform-024-depends-on-and-dynamic-blocks","sec":"terraform-s025","q":"How do you handle dynamic blocks?","a":"<p>A <code>dynamic</code> block loops over nested configuration.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>dynamic &quot;ingress&quot; { \n    for_each = var.rules \n    content { \n        from_port = ingress.value.port \n    } \n}</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"terraform-f0076","card":"q-terraform-025-provisioners-ci-cd-and-approval","sec":"terraform-s026","q":"What is a provisioner, and when should you avoid it?","a":"<p>A provisioner runs scripts after creation. Avoid it for non-idempotent tasks and use Ansible instead.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"terraform-f0077","card":"q-terraform-025-provisioners-ci-cd-and-approval","sec":"terraform-s026","q":"How do you use Terraform with CI/CD?","a":"<p>Automate plan and apply, and secure credentials.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>run: terraform init &amp;&amp; terraform apply -auto-approve</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"terraform-f0078","card":"q-terraform-025-provisioners-ci-cd-and-approval","sec":"terraform-s026","q":"What is the difference between <code>apply</code> and <code>-auto-approve</code>?","a":"<p><code>apply</code> prompts for confirmation. <code>-auto-approve</code> skips the prompt and executes automatically.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"terraform-f0079","card":"q-terraform-026-scale-policy-and-integration","sec":"terraform-s027","q":"How do you handle large-scale infrastructure?","a":"<p>Modules, split state, parallel runs and <code>-target</code>.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"terraform-f0080","card":"q-terraform-026-scale-policy-and-integration","sec":"terraform-s027","q":"What is Terraform Sentinel?","a":"<p>Policy-as-code for Terraform Cloud that blocks non-compliant applies.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"terraform-f0081","card":"q-terraform-026-scale-policy-and-integration","sec":"terraform-s027","q":"How do you integrate Terraform with Ansible or Chef?","a":"<p>Terraform provisions and Ansible configures. Pass outputs such as IPs between them.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"terraform-f0082","card":"q-terraform-026-scale-policy-and-integration","sec":"terraform-s027","q":"How do Terraform and Ansible differ when managing AWS resources through Python?","a":"<p>Terraform is declarative (desired state) and Ansible is procedural (steps). Terraform provisions (for example EC2 instances) and Ansible configures (installing software). Terraform keeps a state file and Ansible is stateless. Python drives Terraform through <code>python-terraform</code> or <code>subprocess</code>, and Ansible through its Python API or custom modules.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"terraform-f0083","card":"q-terraform-027-logging","sec":"terraform-s028","q":"How do you enable detailed logging?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>export TF_LOG=DEBUG</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"terraform-f0084","card":"q-terraform-027-logging","sec":"terraform-s028","q":"What is <code>TF_LOG</code>?","a":"<p>It sets the log level (<code>TRACE</code>, <code>DEBUG</code>, and so on) for debugging.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"terraform-f0085","card":"q-terraform-028-common-errors","sec":"terraform-s029","q":"How do you fix a \"resource already exists\" error?","a":"<p>Import the resource.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>terraform import aws_instance.example i-1234567890abcdef0</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"terraform-f0086","card":"q-terraform-028-common-errors","sec":"terraform-s029","q":"How do you fix a \"provider config not present\" error?","a":"<p>Add the missing provider block and re-run init.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"terraform-f0087","card":"q-terraform-028-common-errors","sec":"terraform-s029","q":"How do you resolve dependency cycle errors?","a":"<p>Refactor references, use data sources, and inspect <code>terraform graph</code>.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"terraform-f0088","card":"q-terraform-028-common-errors","sec":"terraform-s029","q":"Why does <code>terraform plan</code> fail?","a":"<p>Syntax errors, provider issues, conflicts or drift.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"terraform-f0089","card":"q-terraform-029-crashes-and-graph","sec":"terraform-s030","q":"What if Terraform crashes mid-run?","a":"<p>Check the logs, inspect the state, then retry the apply.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"terraform-f0090","card":"q-terraform-029-crashes-and-graph","sec":"terraform-s030","q":"How do you debug a silent module failure?","a":"<p>Check logs, isolate the module, add outputs and run plan.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"terraform-f0091","card":"q-terraform-029-crashes-and-graph","sec":"terraform-s030","q":"What is <code>terraform graph</code>?","a":"<p>It maps dependencies.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>terraform graph | dot -Tpng &gt; graph.png</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"terraform-f0092","card":"q-terraform-030-vpc-terraform-cloud-and-manual-deletion","sec":"terraform-s031","q":"How do you deploy an AWS VPC with subnets?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>module &quot;vpc&quot; { \n    source = &quot;./vpc&quot; \n    public_subnet_cidrs = [&quot;10.0.1.0/24&quot;] \n}</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"terraform-f0093","card":"q-terraform-030-vpc-terraform-cloud-and-manual-deletion","sec":"terraform-s031","q":"How do you migrate to Terraform Cloud?","a":"<p>Add the backend, run init and push the state.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>backend &quot;remote&quot; { \n    organization = &quot;my-org&quot; \n}</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"terraform-f0094","card":"q-terraform-030-vpc-terraform-cloud-and-manual-deletion","sec":"terraform-s031","q":"How do you fix a manually deleted resource?","a":"<p>Run <code>apply</code> to recreate it, or <code>terraform state rm</code> to forget it.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"terraform-f0095","card":"q-terraform-031-high-availability-and-kubernetes","sec":"terraform-s032","q":"How do you build a highly available app across regions?","a":"<p>Use multiple provider aliases and Route 53 failover.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"terraform-f0096","card":"q-terraform-031-high-availability-and-kubernetes","sec":"terraform-s032","q":"How do you automate a Kubernetes cluster?","a":"<p>Use the EKS module with CI/CD.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>resource &quot;aws_eks_cluster&quot; &quot;example&quot; { \n    name = &quot;my-cluster&quot; \n}</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"terraform-f0097","card":"q-terraform-032-rate-limits-and-environment-differences","sec":"terraform-s033","q":"How do you handle a failure caused by rate limits?","a":"<p>Lower <code>-parallelism</code>, retry, and split the configuration.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"terraform-f0098","card":"q-terraform-032-rate-limits-and-environment-differences","sec":"terraform-s033","q":"A config works in dev but fails in prod. What do you do?","a":"<p>Compare variables, logs and permissions, then standardize.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"terraform-f0099","card":"q-terraform-032-rate-limits-and-environment-differences","sec":"terraform-s033","q":"How do you replicate on-prem infrastructure?","a":"<p>Map it to cloud equivalents (VPCs, VMs) and start with a proof of concept.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"terraform-f0100","card":"q-terraform-033-counts-and-conditions","sec":"terraform-s034","q":"How do you create 50 EC2 instances with unique names?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>resource &quot;aws_instance&quot; &quot;example&quot; { \n    count = 50 \n    tags = { \n        Name = &quot;instance-${count.index + 1}&quot; \n    } \n}</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"terraform-f0101","card":"q-terraform-033-counts-and-conditions","sec":"terraform-s034","q":"How do you deploy conditionally by environment?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>count = var.env == &quot;prod&quot; ? 2 : 1</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"terraform-f0102","card":"q-terraform-034-aws","sec":"terraform-s035","q":"How do you configure Terraform for AWS?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>provider &quot;aws&quot; { \n    region = &quot;us-east-1&quot; \n}\nresource &quot;aws_vpc&quot; &quot;main&quot; { \n    cidr_block = &quot;10.0.0.0/16&quot; \n}</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"terraform-f0103","card":"q-terraform-034-aws","sec":"terraform-s035","q":"How do IAM roles differ in Terraform versus the Console?","a":"<p>Terraform is code and repeatable. The Console is manual and quick.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"terraform-f0104","card":"q-terraform-034-aws","sec":"terraform-s035","q":"How do you read secrets from AWS Secrets Manager or Vault?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>data &quot;aws_secretsmanager_secret_version&quot; &quot;secret&quot; { \n    secret_id = &quot;my-secret&quot; \n}</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"terraform-f0105","card":"q-terraform-035-azure-and-gcp","sec":"terraform-s036","q":"How do you create an Azure resource group and VNet?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>resource &quot;azurerm_resource_group&quot; &quot;rg&quot; { \n    name = &quot;my-rg&quot; \n}\nresource &quot;azurerm_virtual_network&quot; &quot;vnet&quot; { \n    name = &quot;my-vnet&quot; \n}</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"terraform-f0106","card":"q-terraform-035-azure-and-gcp","sec":"terraform-s036","q":"How do you create a GCP Compute Engine instance?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>resource &quot;google_compute_instance&quot; &quot;vm&quot; { \n    name = &quot;my-vm&quot; \n    machine_type = &quot;e2-medium&quot; \n}</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"terraform-f0107","card":"q-terraform-036-experience-and-limitations","sec":"terraform-s037","q":"How do you stay updated with Terraform?","a":"<p>Docs, GitHub, blogs and labs.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"terraform-f0108","card":"q-terraform-036-experience-and-limitations","sec":"terraform-s037","q":"What is the most complex infrastructure you have deployed?","a":"<p>A multi-region HA app, with challenges around drift, dependencies and secrets.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"terraform-f0109","card":"q-terraform-036-experience-and-limitations","sec":"terraform-s037","q":"How do you explain Terraform to a newbie?","a":"<p>\"Blueprints for cloud, auto-built.\"</p>","hand":false},{"id":"terraform-f0110","card":"q-terraform-036-experience-and-limitations","sec":"terraform-s037","q":"What are Terraform's limitations?","a":"<p>State fragility and no real-time view. Mitigate with remote state and drift checks.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"terraform-f0111","card":"q-terraform-036-experience-and-limitations","sec":"terraform-s037","q":"How does Terraform compare with other IaC tools?","a":"<p>It is multi-cloud and declarative, versus Ansible (configuration management) and CloudFormation (AWS-only).</p>","hand":false},{"id":"terraform-f0112","card":"q-terraform-037-create-an-ec2-instance-using-terraform","sec":"terraform-s038","q":"In Terraform, which resource type creates an EC2 instance, and which arguments set its AMI, size, key pair and subnet?","a":"<p>The <code>aws_instance</code> resource. <code>ami</code> sets the image, <code>instance_type</code> the size, <code>key_name</code> the key pair and <code>subnet_id</code> the subnet.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>resource &quot;aws_instance&quot; &quot;my_ec2&quot; {\n  ami           = &quot;ami-0c55b159cbfafe1f0&quot;\n  instance_type = &quot;t2.micro&quot;\n  key_name      = &quot;my-key-pair&quot;\n  subnet_id     = &quot;subnet-12345678&quot;\n  security_groups = [&quot;sg-12345678&quot;]\n}</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0113","card":"q-terraform-037-create-an-ec2-instance-using-terraform","sec":"terraform-s038","q":"In an <code>aws_instance</code> block, which argument attaches security groups, and what value shape does it take?","a":"<p><code>security_groups</code> takes a list of security group IDs.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>security_groups = [&quot;sg-12345678&quot;]</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0114","card":"q-terraform-038-attach-a-security-group-to-an-ec2-instan","sec":"terraform-s039","q":"In Terraform, how do you attach a security group defined in the same configuration to an <code>aws_instance</code>?","a":"<p>Reference the security group resource's <code>name</code> attribute inside the <code>security_groups</code> list.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>security_groups = [aws_security_group.my_sg.name]</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0115","card":"q-terraform-038-attach-a-security-group-to-an-ec2-instan","sec":"terraform-s039","q":"Write the Terraform <code>aws_instance</code> that uses the security group <code>aws_security_group.my_sg</code>.","a":"<p>Use the <code>aws_instance</code> resource and point <code>security_groups</code> at the group's name.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>resource &quot;aws_instance&quot; &quot;my_ec2_with_sg&quot; {\n   ami           = &quot;ami-0c55b159cbfafe1f0&quot;\n   instance_type = &quot;t2.micro&quot;\n   subnet_id     = &quot;subnet-12345678&quot;\n   security_groups = [aws_security_group.my_sg.name]\n}</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0116","card":"q-terraform-039-attach-an-iam-role-to-an-ec2-instance-us","sec":"terraform-s040","q":"In Terraform, which resource connects an IAM role to an EC2 instance, and how does it link to the role?","a":"<p>An <code>aws_iam_instance_profile</code>. Its <code>role</code> argument takes the role's name.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>resource &quot;aws_iam_instance_profile&quot; &quot;my_profile&quot; {\n   name = &quot;my-instance-profile&quot;\n   role = aws_iam_role.my_role.name\n}</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0117","card":"q-terraform-039-attach-an-iam-role-to-an-ec2-instance-us","sec":"terraform-s040","q":"Which <code>aws_instance</code> argument attaches an instance profile to an EC2 instance in Terraform?","a":"<p><code>iam_instance_profile</code>, set to the profile's name.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>iam_instance_profile = aws_iam_instance_profile.my_profile.name</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0118","card":"q-terraform-039-attach-an-iam-role-to-an-ec2-instance-us","sec":"terraform-s040","q":"In Terraform, what are the two resources needed to give an EC2 instance an IAM role, in order of reference?","a":"<p>First an <code>aws_iam_instance_profile</code> that references the role. Then an <code>aws_instance</code> that references the profile through <code>iam_instance_profile</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>resource &quot;aws_instance&quot; &quot;my_ec2_with_role&quot; {\n   ami                  = &quot;ami-0c55b159cbfafe1f0&quot;\n   instance_type        = &quot;t2.micro&quot;\n   subnet_id            = &quot;subnet-12345678&quot;\n   iam_instance_profile = aws_iam_instance_profile.my_profile.name\n}</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0119","card":"q-terraform-040-create-an-ebs-volume-and-attach-it-to-an","sec":"terraform-s041","q":"In Terraform, which resource creates an EBS volume, and which arguments set its zone, size and type?","a":"<p>The <code>aws_ebs_volume</code> resource. <code>availability_zone</code>, <code>size</code> and <code>type</code> set those values.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>resource &quot;aws_ebs_volume&quot; &quot;my_volume&quot; {\n  availability_zone = &quot;us-east-1a&quot;\n  size              = 10\n  type              = &quot;gp3&quot;\n}</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0120","card":"q-terraform-040-create-an-ebs-volume-and-attach-it-to-an","sec":"terraform-s041","q":"In Terraform, which resource attaches an EBS volume to an EC2 instance, and which arguments does it need?","a":"<p>The <code>aws_volume_attachment</code> resource. It needs <code>device_name</code>, <code>volume_id</code> and <code>instance_id</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>resource &quot;aws_volume_attachment&quot; &quot;my_attachment&quot; {\n  device_name = &quot;/dev/xvdf&quot;\n  volume_id   = aws_ebs_volume.my_volume.id\n  instance_id = aws_instance.my_ec2.id\n}</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0121","card":"q-terraform-041-create-an-auto-scaling-group-using-terra","sec":"terraform-s042","q":"In Terraform, what do you create before an <code>aws_autoscaling_group</code>, and what does it define?","a":"<p>An <code>aws_launch_template</code>. It defines the image and instance type for the group's instances.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>resource &quot;aws_launch_template&quot; &quot;my_lt&quot; {\n   name_prefix   = &quot;my-lt&quot;\n   image_id      = &quot;ami-0c55b159cbfafe1f0&quot;\n   instance_type = &quot;t2.micro&quot;\n}</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0122","card":"q-terraform-041-create-an-auto-scaling-group-using-terra","sec":"terraform-s042","q":"Which arguments set the minimum, maximum and desired size of a Terraform <code>aws_autoscaling_group</code>, and which subnets does it use?","a":"<p><code>min_size</code>, <code>max_size</code> and <code>desired_capacity</code> set the sizes. <code>vpc_zone_identifier</code> lists the subnets.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>min_size            = 1\nmax_size            = 3\ndesired_capacity    = 2\nvpc_zone_identifier = [&quot;subnet-12345678&quot;, &quot;subnet-87654321&quot;]</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0123","card":"q-terraform-041-create-an-auto-scaling-group-using-terra","sec":"terraform-s042","q":"How does a Terraform <code>aws_autoscaling_group</code> reference its launch template and always use the newest version?","a":"<p>A <code>launch_template</code> block with the template's <code>id</code> and <code>version</code> set to <code>\"$Latest\"</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>launch_template {\n  id      = aws_launch_template.my_lt.id\n  version = &quot;$Latest&quot;\n}</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0124","card":"q-terraform-042-create-an-rds-instance-using-terraform","sec":"terraform-s043","q":"In Terraform, which resource creates an RDS instance?","a":"<p>The <code>aws_db_instance</code> resource.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>resource &quot;aws_db_instance&quot; &quot;my_rds&quot; {\n  identifier          = &quot;my-rds-instance&quot;\n  engine              = &quot;mysql&quot;\n  instance_class      = &quot;db.t3.micro&quot;\n  allocated_storage   = 20\n}</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0125","card":"q-terraform-042-create-an-rds-instance-using-terraform","sec":"terraform-s043","q":"In an <code>aws_db_instance</code> block, which arguments set the engine, instance class and storage?","a":"<p><code>engine</code> sets the engine (<code>mysql</code>), <code>instance_class</code> the class (<code>db.t3.micro</code>) and <code>allocated_storage</code> the storage (<code>20</code>).</p>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0126","card":"q-terraform-042-create-an-rds-instance-using-terraform","sec":"terraform-s043","q":"In an <code>aws_db_instance</code> block, which arguments set the admin credentials?","a":"<p><code>username</code> and <code>password</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>username            = &quot;admin&quot;\npassword            = &quot;MySecurePassword123&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0127","card":"q-terraform-042-create-an-rds-instance-using-terraform","sec":"terraform-s043","q":"Which <code>aws_db_instance</code> arguments place the database in a security group and a subnet group?","a":"<p><code>vpc_security_group_ids</code> for security groups and <code>db_subnet_group_name</code> for the subnet group.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>vpc_security_group_ids = [&quot;sg-12345678&quot;]\ndb_subnet_group_name = &quot;my-subnet-group&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0128","card":"q-terraform-043-attach-a-security-group-to-an-rds-instan","sec":"terraform-s044","q":"In Terraform, how do you attach a security group to an RDS instance?","a":"<p>Set <code>vpc_security_group_ids</code> on the <code>aws_db_instance</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>vpc_security_group_ids = [&quot;sg-12345678&quot;]</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0129","card":"q-terraform-043-attach-a-security-group-to-an-rds-instan","sec":"terraform-s044","q":"Besides <code>vpc_security_group_ids</code>, which argument do you set on an <code>aws_db_instance</code> when attaching a security group?","a":"<p><code>db_subnet_group_name</code>, set to the subnet group's name.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>db_subnet_group_name = &quot;my-subnet-group&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0130","card":"q-terraform-044-create-an-rds-snapshot-using-terraform","sec":"terraform-s045","q":"In Terraform, which resource creates an RDS snapshot?","a":"<p>The <code>aws_db_snapshot</code> resource.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0131","card":"q-terraform-044-create-an-rds-snapshot-using-terraform","sec":"terraform-s045","q":"Which two arguments does an <code>aws_db_snapshot</code> need in Terraform?","a":"<p><code>db_instance_identifier</code> names the instance to snapshot. <code>db_snapshot_identifier</code> names the snapshot.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>resource &quot;aws_db_snapshot&quot; &quot;my_rds_snapshot&quot; {\n    db_instance_identifier = &quot;my-rds-instance&quot;\n    db_snapshot_identifier = &quot;my-rds-snapshot&quot;\n}</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0132","card":"q-terraform-045-create-an-s3-bucket-using-terraform","sec":"terraform-s046","q":"In Terraform, which resource creates an S3 bucket, and which argument is needed at minimum?","a":"<p>The <code>aws_s3_bucket</code> resource. The <code>bucket</code> argument sets the unique bucket name.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>resource &quot;aws_s3_bucket&quot; &quot;my_bucket&quot; {\n  bucket = &quot;my-unique-bucket-name&quot;\n}</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0133","card":"q-terraform-046-create-a-dynamodb-table-using-terraform","sec":"terraform-s047","q":"In Terraform, which resource creates a DynamoDB table?","a":"<p>The <code>aws_dynamodb_table</code> resource.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0134","card":"q-terraform-046-create-a-dynamodb-table-using-terraform","sec":"terraform-s047","q":"In a Terraform <code>aws_dynamodb_table</code>, how do you set on-demand billing?","a":"<p>Set <code>billing_mode</code> to <code>\"PAY_PER_REQUEST\"</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>billing_mode   = &quot;PAY_PER_REQUEST&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0135","card":"q-terraform-046-create-a-dynamodb-table-using-terraform","sec":"terraform-s047","q":"In a Terraform <code>aws_dynamodb_table</code>, how do you define the partition key <code>id</code> as a string?","a":"<p>Set <code>hash_key = \"id\"</code> and add an <code>attribute</code> block with the name <code>id</code> and type <code>S</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>hash_key       = &quot;id&quot;\nattribute {\n    name = &quot;id&quot;\n    type = &quot;S&quot;\n}</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0136","card":"q-terraform-047-create-a-vpc-using-terraform","sec":"terraform-s048","q":"In Terraform, which resource creates a VPC and which argument sets its IP range?","a":"<p>The <code>aws_vpc</code> resource. <code>cidr_block</code> sets the range, for example <code>10.0.0.0/16</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>resource &quot;aws_vpc&quot; &quot;my_vpc&quot; {\n  cidr_block = &quot;10.0.0.0/16&quot;\n  tags = {\n     Name = &quot;my-vpc&quot;\n  }\n}</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0137","card":"q-terraform-047-create-a-vpc-using-terraform","sec":"terraform-s048","q":"How do you give a Terraform <code>aws_vpc</code> a name?","a":"<p>Add a <code>tags</code> map with the key <code>Name</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>tags = {\n   Name = &quot;my-vpc&quot;\n}</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0138","card":"q-terraform-048-attach-a-subnet-to-a-vpc-using-terraform","sec":"terraform-s049","q":"In Terraform, which resource creates a subnet and how does it attach to a VPC?","a":"<p>The <code>aws_subnet</code> resource. Its <code>vpc_id</code> references the VPC's <code>id</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>vpc_id     = aws_vpc.my_vpc.id</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0139","card":"q-terraform-048-attach-a-subnet-to-a-vpc-using-terraform","sec":"terraform-s049","q":"Which arguments set the IP range and zone of a Terraform <code>aws_subnet</code>?","a":"<p><code>cidr_block</code> sets the range and <code>availability_zone</code> sets the zone.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>resource &quot;aws_subnet&quot; &quot;my_subnet&quot; {\n   vpc_id     = aws_vpc.my_vpc.id\n   cidr_block = &quot;10.0.1.0/24&quot;\n   availability_zone = &quot;us-east-1a&quot;\n}</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0140","card":"q-terraform-049-attach-an-internet-gateway-to-a-vpc-usin","sec":"terraform-s050","q":"In Terraform, which resource creates an internet gateway and attaches it to a VPC?","a":"<p>The <code>aws_internet_gateway</code> resource. Its <code>vpc_id</code> argument names the VPC.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>resource &quot;aws_internet_gateway&quot; &quot;my_igw&quot; {\n    vpc_id = &quot;vpc-12345678&quot;\n}</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0141","card":"q-terraform-050-attach-a-route-table-to-a-subnet-using-t","sec":"terraform-s051","q":"In Terraform, how do you create a route table that sends all internet traffic to an internet gateway?","a":"<p>Use <code>aws_route_table</code> with a <code>route</code> block. The <code>cidr_block</code> is <code>0.0.0.0/0</code> and <code>gateway_id</code> references the gateway.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>resource &quot;aws_route_table&quot; &quot;my_route_table&quot; {\n    vpc_id = &quot;vpc-12345678&quot;\n    route {\n        cidr_block = &quot;0.0.0.0/0&quot;\n        gateway_id = aws_internet_gateway.my_igw.id\n    }\n}</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0142","card":"q-terraform-050-attach-a-route-table-to-a-subnet-using-t","sec":"terraform-s051","q":"In Terraform, which resource attaches a route table to a subnet, and which arguments does it need?","a":"<p>The <code>aws_route_table_association</code> resource. It needs <code>subnet_id</code> and <code>route_table_id</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>resource &quot;aws_route_table_association&quot; &quot;my_route_table_assoc&quot; {\n    subnet_id      = &quot;subnet-12345678&quot;\n    route_table_id = aws_route_table.my_route_table.id\n}</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0143","card":"q-terraform-051-create-a-security-group-using-terraform","sec":"terraform-s052","q":"In Terraform, which resource creates a security group, and which arguments identify it?","a":"<p>The <code>aws_security_group</code> resource. <code>name</code>, <code>description</code> and <code>vpc_id</code> identify it.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>name        = &quot;my-security-group&quot;\ndescription = &quot;My security group&quot;\nvpc_id      = &quot;vpc-12345678&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0144","card":"q-terraform-051-create-a-security-group-using-terraform","sec":"terraform-s052","q":"In a Terraform <code>aws_security_group</code>, how do you allow SSH from anywhere?","a":"<p>Add an <code>ingress</code> block for port 22 over <code>tcp</code> with <code>cidr_blocks</code> set to <code>0.0.0.0/0</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>ingress {\n   from_port   = 22\n   to_port     = 22\n   protocol    = &quot;tcp&quot;\n   cidr_blocks = [&quot;0.0.0.0/0&quot;]\n}</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0145","card":"q-terraform-052-create-an-elastic-ip-and-attach-it-to-an","sec":"terraform-s053","q":"In Terraform, which resource allocates an Elastic IP?","a":"<p>The <code>aws_eip</code> resource, with <code>vpc = true</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>resource &quot;aws_eip&quot; &quot;my_eip&quot; {\n    vpc = true\n}</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0146","card":"q-terraform-052-create-an-elastic-ip-and-attach-it-to-an","sec":"terraform-s053","q":"In Terraform, which resource attaches an Elastic IP to an EC2 instance, and which arguments does it need?","a":"<p>The <code>aws_eip_association</code> resource. It needs <code>instance_id</code> and <code>allocation_id</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>resource &quot;aws_eip_association&quot; &quot;eip_assoc&quot; {\n    instance_id   = &quot;i-1234567890abcdef0&quot;\n    allocation_id = aws_eip.my_eip.id\n}</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0147","card":"q-terraform-053-create-a-load-balancer-using-terraform","sec":"terraform-s054","q":"In Terraform, which resource creates a load balancer?","a":"<p>The <code>aws_lb</code> resource.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0148","card":"q-terraform-053-create-a-load-balancer-using-terraform","sec":"terraform-s054","q":"In a Terraform <code>aws_lb</code>, how do you make an internet-facing Application Load Balancer?","a":"<p>Set <code>internal = false</code> and <code>load_balancer_type = \"application\"</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>internal           = false\nload_balancer_type = &quot;application&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0149","card":"q-terraform-053-create-a-load-balancer-using-terraform","sec":"terraform-s054","q":"Which arguments attach security groups and subnets to a Terraform <code>aws_lb</code>?","a":"<p><code>security_groups</code> and <code>subnets</code>, both lists of IDs.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>security_groups    = [&quot;sg-12345678&quot;]\nsubnets            = [&quot;subnet-12345678&quot;, &quot;subnet-87654321&quot;]</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0150","card":"q-terraform-054-create-a-route-53-record-using-terraform","sec":"terraform-s055","q":"In Terraform, which resource creates a Route 53 DNS record?","a":"<p>The <code>aws_route53_record</code> resource.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0151","card":"q-terraform-054-create-a-route-53-record-using-terraform","sec":"terraform-s055","q":"Which arguments define a Terraform <code>aws_route53_record</code> for <code>www.example.com</code> pointing to an IP?","a":"<p><code>zone_id</code> is the hosted zone. <code>name</code> is the domain, <code>type</code> is the record type, <code>ttl</code> is the cache time and <code>records</code> lists the values.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>resource &quot;aws_route53_record&quot; &quot;my_record&quot; {\n    zone_id = &quot;Z1234567890ABCDEF&quot;\n    name    = &quot;www.example.com&quot;\n    type    = &quot;A&quot;\n    ttl     = 300\n    records = [&quot;192.0.2.1&quot;]\n}</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0152","card":"q-terraform-055-create-an-iam-role-using-terraform","sec":"terraform-s056","q":"In Terraform, which resource creates an IAM role, and which argument defines who can assume it?","a":"<p>The <code>aws_iam_role</code> resource. <code>assume_role_policy</code> defines who can assume it, usually written with <code>jsonencode</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>resource &quot;aws_iam_role&quot; &quot;my_role&quot; {\n  name = &quot;my-iam-role&quot;\n}</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0153","card":"q-terraform-055-create-an-iam-role-using-terraform","sec":"terraform-s056","q":"In a Terraform IAM role, how do you let EC2 assume the role?","a":"<p>Set a statement with <code>Action = \"sts:AssumeRole\"</code>, <code>Effect = \"Allow\"</code> and the principal service <code>ec2.amazonaws.com</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>Action = &quot;sts:AssumeRole&quot;\nEffect = &quot;Allow&quot;\nPrincipal = {\n  Service = &quot;ec2.amazonaws.com&quot;\n}</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0154","card":"q-terraform-055-create-an-iam-role-using-terraform","sec":"terraform-s056","q":"In Terraform, which resource attaches a managed policy to an IAM role?","a":"<p>The <code>aws_iam_role_policy_attachment</code> resource. It needs <code>role</code> and <code>policy_arn</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>resource &quot;aws_iam_role_policy_attachment&quot; &quot;my_role_policy&quot; {\n  role       = aws_iam_role.my_role.name\n  policy_arn = &quot;arn:aws:iam::aws:policy/AmazonS3ReadOnlyAccess&quot;\n}</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0155","card":"q-terraform-056-create-a-lambda-function-using-terraform","sec":"terraform-s057","q":"In Terraform, which resource creates a Lambda function?","a":"<p>The <code>aws_lambda_function</code> resource.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0156","card":"q-terraform-056-create-a-lambda-function-using-terraform","sec":"terraform-s057","q":"Which arguments set the name, entry point, runtime and execution role of a Terraform <code>aws_lambda_function</code>?","a":"<p><code>function_name</code>, <code>handler</code>, <code>runtime</code> and <code>role</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>function_name = &quot;my-lambda-function&quot;\nhandler       = &quot;index.handler&quot;\nruntime       = &quot;nodejs18.x&quot;\nrole          = &quot;arn:aws:iam::123456789012:role/lambda-exec-role&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0157","card":"q-terraform-056-create-a-lambda-function-using-terraform","sec":"terraform-s057","q":"How does a Terraform <code>aws_lambda_function</code> load its code from S3?","a":"<p>Set <code>s3_bucket</code> to the bucket and <code>s3_key</code> to the zip file's key.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>s3_bucket     = &quot;my-code-bucket&quot;\ns3_key        = &quot;lambda-code.zip&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0158","card":"q-terraform-057-create-an-sns-topic-using-terraform","sec":"terraform-s058","q":"In Terraform, which resource creates an SNS topic?","a":"<p>The <code>aws_sns_topic</code> resource, with a <code>name</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>resource &quot;aws_sns_topic&quot; &quot;my_topic&quot; {\n  name = &quot;my-sns-topic&quot;\n}</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0159","card":"q-terraform-058-attach-a-lambda-function-to-an-sns-topic","sec":"terraform-s059","q":"In Terraform, which four resources connect a Lambda function to an SNS topic?","a":"<p><code>aws_sns_topic</code>, <code>aws_lambda_function</code>, <code>aws_sns_topic_subscription</code> and <code>aws_lambda_permission</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0160","card":"q-terraform-058-attach-a-lambda-function-to-an-sns-topic","sec":"terraform-s059","q":"In Terraform, how does an <code>aws_sns_topic_subscription</code> subscribe a Lambda function to a topic?","a":"<p>Set <code>topic_arn</code> to the topic's ARN, <code>protocol</code> to <code>\"lambda\"</code> and <code>endpoint</code> to the function's ARN.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>resource &quot;aws_sns_topic_subscription&quot; &quot;lambda_sns&quot; {\n    topic_arn = aws_sns_topic.my_sns_topic.arn\n    protocol  = &quot;lambda&quot;\n    endpoint  = aws_lambda_function.my_lambda.arn\n}</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0161","card":"q-terraform-058-attach-a-lambda-function-to-an-sns-topic","sec":"terraform-s059","q":"In Terraform, why do you add an <code>aws_lambda_permission</code> when connecting SNS to Lambda, and what does it set?","a":"<p>It allows SNS to invoke the function. It sets <code>action</code> to <code>lambda:InvokeFunction</code>, <code>principal</code> to <code>sns.amazonaws.com</code> and <code>source_arn</code> to the topic's ARN.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>resource &quot;aws_lambda_permission&quot; &quot;sns_invoke&quot; {\n    statement_id  = &quot;AllowExecutionFromSNS&quot;\n    action        = &quot;lambda:InvokeFunction&quot;\n    function_name = aws_lambda_function.my_lambda.function_name\n    principal     = &quot;sns.amazonaws.com&quot;\n    source_arn    = aws_sns_topic.my_sns_topic.arn\n}</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0162","card":"q-terraform-058-attach-a-lambda-function-to-an-sns-topic","sec":"terraform-s059","q":"In the Terraform SNS-to-Lambda setup, how does the Lambda function load its code?","a":"<p>It uses <code>filename</code> pointing to the local zip file.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>filename      = &quot;lambda-code.zip&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0163","card":"q-terraform-059-create-an-ecs-cluster-using-terraform","sec":"terraform-s060","q":"In Terraform, which resource creates an ECS cluster?","a":"<p>The <code>aws_ecs_cluster</code> resource, with a <code>name</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>resource &quot;aws_ecs_cluster&quot; &quot;my_ecs_cluster&quot; {\n    name = &quot;my-ecs-cluster&quot;\n}</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0164","card":"q-terraform-060-create-a-task-definition-and-attach-it-t","sec":"terraform-s061","q":"In Terraform, which resource defines an ECS task, and which arguments make it a Fargate task?","a":"<p>The <code>aws_ecs_task_definition</code> resource. Set <code>network_mode = \"awsvpc\"</code> and <code>requires_compatibilities = [\"FARGATE\"]</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>network_mode             = &quot;awsvpc&quot;\nrequires_compatibilities = [&quot;FARGATE&quot;]</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0165","card":"q-terraform-060-create-a-task-definition-and-attach-it-t","sec":"terraform-s061","q":"Which arguments set the CPU, memory and execution role of a Terraform <code>aws_ecs_task_definition</code>?","a":"<p><code>cpu</code>, <code>memory</code> and <code>execution_role_arn</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>cpu                      = &quot;256&quot;\nmemory                   = &quot;512&quot;\nexecution_role_arn       = &quot;arn:aws:iam::123456789012:role/ecs-task-execution-role&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0166","card":"q-terraform-060-create-a-task-definition-and-attach-it-t","sec":"terraform-s061","q":"In a Terraform <code>aws_ecs_task_definition</code>, how do you define the container and expose port 80?","a":"<p>Use <code>container_definitions</code> with <code>jsonencode</code>, and a <code>portMappings</code> entry in the container.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>container_definitions    = jsonencode([{\n    name  = &quot;my-container&quot;\n    image = &quot;amazon/amazon-ecs-sample&quot;\n    essential = true\n    portMappings = [{\n        containerPort = 80\n        hostPort      = 80\n    }]\n}])</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0167","card":"q-terraform-060-create-a-task-definition-and-attach-it-t","sec":"terraform-s061","q":"In Terraform, which resource attaches a task definition to an ECS cluster and runs it?","a":"<p>The <code>aws_ecs_service</code> resource. <code>cluster</code> references the cluster's id and <code>task_definition</code> references the task's ARN.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>cluster         = aws_ecs_cluster.my_ecs_cluster.id\ntask_definition = aws_ecs_task_definition.my_task.arn</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0168","card":"q-terraform-060-create-a-task-definition-and-attach-it-t","sec":"terraform-s061","q":"In a Terraform <code>aws_ecs_service</code>, which arguments set the launch type and the number of tasks?","a":"<p><code>launch_type = \"FARGATE\"</code> and <code>desired_count = 1</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>launch_type     = &quot;FARGATE&quot;\ndesired_count   = 1</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0169","card":"q-terraform-060-create-a-task-definition-and-attach-it-t","sec":"terraform-s061","q":"In a Terraform <code>aws_ecs_service</code> on Fargate, how do you set the network?","a":"<p>Use a <code>network_configuration</code> block with <code>subnets</code>, <code>security_groups</code> and <code>assign_public_ip</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>network_configuration {\n    subnets          = [&quot;subnet-12345678&quot;]\n    security_groups  = [&quot;sg-12345678&quot;]\n    assign_public_ip = true\n}</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0170","card":"q-terraform-061-create-a-cloudwatch-alarm-for-an-ec2-ins","sec":"terraform-s062","q":"In Terraform, which resource creates a CloudWatch alarm?","a":"<p>The <code>aws_cloudwatch_metric_alarm</code> resource.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0171","card":"q-terraform-061-create-a-cloudwatch-alarm-for-an-ec2-ins","sec":"terraform-s062","q":"In a Terraform CloudWatch alarm for EC2 CPU, which arguments select the metric?","a":"<p><code>metric_name = \"CPUUtilization\"</code>, <code>namespace = \"AWS/EC2\"</code> and <code>statistic = \"Average\"</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>metric_name         = &quot;CPUUtilization&quot;\nnamespace           = &quot;AWS/EC2&quot;\nstatistic           = &quot;Average&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0172","card":"q-terraform-061-create-a-cloudwatch-alarm-for-an-ec2-ins","sec":"terraform-s062","q":"In a Terraform CloudWatch alarm, which arguments set when the alarm fires?","a":"<p><code>comparison_operator</code>, <code>threshold</code>, <code>period</code> and <code>evaluation_periods</code>. This alarm fires when the average is above 80 over 2 periods of 300 seconds.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>comparison_operator = &quot;GreaterThanThreshold&quot;\nevaluation_periods  = 2\nperiod              = 300\nthreshold           = 80</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0173","card":"q-terraform-061-create-a-cloudwatch-alarm-for-an-ec2-ins","sec":"terraform-s062","q":"In a Terraform CloudWatch alarm, how do you notify an SNS topic and target one EC2 instance?","a":"<p><code>alarm_actions</code> lists the topic ARN. The <code>dimensions</code> map sets <code>InstanceId</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>alarm_actions       = [&quot;arn:aws:sns:us-east-1:123456789012:my-topic&quot;]\ndimensions = {\n    InstanceId = &quot;i-1234567890abcdef0&quot;\n}</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0174","card":"q-terraform-062-nginx-on-ec2-with-ubuntu-20-04-lts","sec":"terraform-s063","q":"What does the Terraform stack for Nginx on Ubuntu 20.04 on EC2 deploy?","a":"<p>An EC2 instance running Nginx, with a VPC, subnet, internet gateway, route table, security group and user data tailored for Ubuntu.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0175","card":"q-terraform-062-nginx-on-ec2-with-ubuntu-20-04-lts","sec":"terraform-s063","q":"In the Terraform Nginx-on-Ubuntu stack, which ingress and egress rules does the security group have?","a":"<p>Ingress on port 80 and port 22 over <code>tcp</code> from <code>0.0.0.0/0</code>. Egress allows all traffic.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>egress {\n    from_port   = 0\n    to_port     = 0\n    protocol    = &quot;-1&quot;\n    cidr_blocks = [&quot;0.0.0.0/0&quot;]\n}</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0176","card":"q-terraform-062-nginx-on-ec2-with-ubuntu-20-04-lts","sec":"terraform-s063","q":"In the Terraform Nginx-on-Ubuntu stack, how does the route table give the subnet internet access?","a":"<p>A route sends <code>0.0.0.0/0</code> to the internet gateway, and a route table association links the table to the subnet.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>resource &quot;aws_route_table_association&quot; &quot;nginx_route_assoc&quot; {\n    subnet_id      = aws_subnet.nginx_subnet.id\n    route_table_id = aws_route_table.nginx_route_table.id\n}</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0177","card":"q-terraform-062-nginx-on-ec2-with-ubuntu-20-04-lts","sec":"terraform-s063","q":"In the Terraform Nginx-on-Ubuntu stack, what user data installs and starts Nginx?","a":"<p>A bash script that uses <code>apt-get</code>, then starts and enables Nginx with <code>systemctl</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>#!/bin/bash\napt-get update -y\napt-get install -y nginx\nsystemctl start nginx\nsystemctl enable nginx</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0178","card":"q-terraform-062-nginx-on-ec2-with-ubuntu-20-04-lts","sec":"terraform-s063","q":"Which AMI does the Terraform Nginx-on-Ubuntu stack use, and what do you do for other regions?","a":"<p><code>ami-0e86e20dae9224db8</code>, Ubuntu 20.04 LTS in <code>us-east-1</code>. Replace it for other regions.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0179","card":"q-terraform-062-nginx-on-ec2-with-ubuntu-20-04-lts","sec":"terraform-s063","q":"Which <code>aws_instance</code> argument gives the Nginx EC2 instance a public IP in Terraform?","a":"<p><code>associate_public_ip_address = true</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>associate_public_ip_address = true</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0180","card":"q-terraform-062-nginx-on-ec2-with-ubuntu-20-04-lts","sec":"terraform-s063","q":"In the Terraform Nginx-on-Ubuntu stack, how do you reach Nginx after <code>terraform apply</code>, and what must you replace for SSH?","a":"<p>Open <code>http://&lt;public-ip&gt;</code>. Replace <code>my-key-pair</code> with your actual key pair name.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0181","card":"q-terraform-063-nginx-on-ec2-with-centos-7","sec":"terraform-s064","q":"What changes between the Terraform Nginx-on-Ubuntu stack and the CentOS 7 stack?","a":"<p>The network resources are identical. Only the AMI and user data change.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0182","card":"q-terraform-063-nginx-on-ec2-with-centos-7","sec":"terraform-s064","q":"Which AMI does the Terraform Nginx-on-CentOS 7 stack use?","a":"<p><code>ami-0b2c7a2f6f2d513d4</code>, CentOS 7 in <code>us-east-1</code>. Update it for other regions.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0183","card":"q-terraform-063-nginx-on-ec2-with-centos-7","sec":"terraform-s064","q":"In the Terraform Nginx-on-CentOS 7 stack, what user data installs and starts Nginx?","a":"<p>A bash script that uses <code>yum</code>, installs <code>epel-release</code> first, then installs Nginx and starts and enables it.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>#!/bin/bash\nyum update -y\nyum install -y epel-release\nyum install -y nginx\nsystemctl start nginx\nsystemctl enable nginx</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0184","card":"q-terraform-063-nginx-on-ec2-with-centos-7","sec":"terraform-s064","q":"Why does the CentOS 7 Nginx user data install <code>epel-release</code> first?","a":"<p>The EPEL repository provides Nginx. On CentOS use <code>yum install -y nginx</code> instead of <code>apt-get</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0185","card":"q-terraform-064-connecting-an-rds-instance-to-an-ec2-ins","sec":"terraform-s065","q":"How does an EC2 instance reach an RDS instance in the Terraform stack that connects them?","a":"<p>Over the network, using security groups and a VPC.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0186","card":"q-terraform-064-connecting-an-rds-instance-to-an-ec2-ins","sec":"terraform-s065","q":"In the Terraform stack connecting RDS to EC2, how does the RDS security group allow only the EC2 instance to connect?","a":"<p>Its ingress rule allows port 3306 over <code>tcp</code> from the EC2 security group, using <code>security_groups</code> instead of CIDR blocks.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>ingress {\n    from_port       = 3306\n    to_port         = 3306\n    protocol        = &quot;tcp&quot;\n    security_groups = [aws_security_group.ec2_sg.id]\n}</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0187","card":"q-terraform-064-connecting-an-rds-instance-to-an-ec2-ins","sec":"terraform-s065","q":"In the Terraform stack connecting RDS to EC2, what does the EC2 security group allow?","a":"<p>Outbound traffic. It has an egress rule for all protocols to <code>0.0.0.0/0</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>resource &quot;aws_security_group&quot; &quot;ec2_sg&quot; {\n    vpc_id = aws_vpc.my_vpc.id\n    egress {\n        from_port   = 0\n        to_port     = 0\n        protocol    = &quot;-1&quot;\n        cidr_blocks = [&quot;0.0.0.0/0&quot;]\n    }\n}</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0188","card":"q-terraform-064-connecting-an-rds-instance-to-an-ec2-ins","sec":"terraform-s065","q":"In Terraform, which resource tells an RDS instance which subnets to use?","a":"<p>The <code>aws_db_subnet_group</code> resource, with <code>subnet_ids</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>resource &quot;aws_db_subnet_group&quot; &quot;my_subnet_group&quot; {\n    name       = &quot;my-subnet-group&quot;\n    subnet_ids = [aws_subnet.my_subnet.id]\n}</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0189","card":"q-terraform-065-connecting-an-rds-instance-to-an-ec2-ins","sec":"terraform-s065","q":"In the Terraform stack connecting RDS to EC2, how does the <code>aws_db_instance</code> use the security group and subnet group?","a":"<p><code>vpc_security_group_ids</code> references the RDS security group and <code>db_subnet_group_name</code> references the subnet group's name.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>vpc_security_group_ids = [aws_security_group.rds_sg.id]\ndb_subnet_group_name = aws_db_subnet_group.my_subnet_group.name</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0190","card":"q-terraform-065-connecting-an-rds-instance-to-an-ec2-ins","sec":"terraform-s065","q":"In the Terraform stack connecting RDS to EC2, how is the EC2 instance placed?","a":"<p>In the same subnet, with its own security group.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>subnet_id     = aws_subnet.my_subnet.id\nsecurity_groups = [aws_security_group.ec2_sg.name]</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0191","card":"q-terraform-065-connecting-an-rds-instance-to-an-ec2-ins","sec":"terraform-s065","q":"What are the five steps of the Terraform stack that connects an RDS instance to an EC2 instance?","a":"<ol>\n  <li>VPC and subnet. 2. Security groups. 3. RDS subnet group. 4. RDS instance. 5. EC2 instance in the same subnet.</li>\n</ol>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0192","card":"q-terraform-065-connecting-an-rds-instance-to-an-ec2-ins","sec":"terraform-s065","q":"How do you connect from the EC2 instance to the RDS instance in this Terraform stack?","a":"<p>Use the RDS endpoint, port <code>3306</code>, and the username and password. An example endpoint is <code>my-rds-instance.abcdef123456.us-east-1.rds.amazonaws.com</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0193","card":"q-terraform-066-auto-scaling-with-cloudwatch-alarms","sec":"terraform-s066","q":"What does the Terraform Auto Scaling with CloudWatch alarms stack contain?","a":"<p>A launch template with the CloudWatch agent, an Auto Scaling group, a step scaling policy, and CPU and memory alarms that trigger it.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0194","card":"q-terraform-066-auto-scaling-with-cloudwatch-alarms","sec":"terraform-s066","q":"In the Terraform Auto Scaling stack, how do you use the default VPC and its subnets?","a":"<p>A <code>data \"aws_vpc\"</code> block with <code>default = true</code>, and a <code>data \"aws_subnets\"</code> block that filters on the VPC id.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>data &quot;aws_vpc&quot; &quot;default&quot; {\n    default = true\n}\n\ndata &quot;aws_subnets&quot; &quot;default&quot; {\n    filter {\n        name   = &quot;vpc-id&quot;\n        values = [data.aws_vpc.default.id]\n    }\n}</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0195","card":"q-terraform-066-auto-scaling-with-cloudwatch-alarms","sec":"terraform-s066","q":"In the Terraform Auto Scaling stack, how does the launch template get a public IP and security group?","a":"<p>A <code>network_interfaces</code> block with <code>associate_public_ip_address = true</code> and the security group's id.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>network_interfaces {\n    associate_public_ip_address = true\n    security_groups             = [aws_security_group.web_sg.id]\n}</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0196","card":"q-terraform-066-auto-scaling-with-cloudwatch-alarms","sec":"terraform-s066","q":"In the Terraform Auto Scaling stack, how does the launch template user data install the CloudWatch agent?","a":"<p>It is wrapped in <code>base64encode</code>, and runs <code>yum install -y amazon-cloudwatch-agent</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>user_data = base64encode(&lt;&lt;-EOF\n#!/bin/bash\nyum install -y amazon-cloudwatch-agent</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0197","card":"q-terraform-066-auto-scaling-with-cloudwatch-alarms","sec":"terraform-s066","q":"In the Terraform Auto Scaling stack, how does the CloudWatch agent report memory?","a":"<p>The user data writes a config that collects <code>mem_used_percent</code> into the <code>CWAgent</code> namespace, then loads it with <code>amazon-cloudwatch-agent-ctl</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>echo &#x27;{&quot;metrics&quot;:{&quot;namespace&quot;:&quot;CWAgent&quot;,&quot;metrics_collected&quot;:{&quot;mem&quot;:{&quot;measurement&quot;:[&quot;mem_used_percent&quot;]}}}}&#x27; &gt; /opt/aws/amazon-cloudwatch-agent/etc/amazon-cloudwatch-agent.json\n/opt/aws/amazon-cloudwatch-agent/bin/amazon-cloudwatch-agent-ctl -a fetch-config -m ec2 -s -c file:/opt/aws/amazon-cloudwatch-agent/etc/amazon-cloudwatch-agent.json</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0198","card":"q-terraform-066-auto-scaling-with-cloudwatch-alarms","sec":"terraform-s066","q":"What size limits does the Auto Scaling group have in the Terraform Auto Scaling stack?","a":"<p>Minimum 1, maximum 4 and desired capacity 2.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>min_size            = 1\nmax_size            = 4\ndesired_capacity    = 2</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0199","card":"q-terraform-066-auto-scaling-with-cloudwatch-alarms","sec":"terraform-s066","q":"In the Terraform Auto Scaling stack, which rules does the web security group have?","a":"<p>Inbound TCP 80 and TCP 22 from <code>0.0.0.0/0</code>, and all outbound traffic (protocol <code>-1</code>).</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>ingress {\n    from_port   = 80\n    to_port     = 80\n    protocol    = &quot;tcp&quot;\n    cidr_blocks = [&quot;0.0.0.0/0&quot;]\n}\ningress {\n    from_port   = 22\n    to_port     = 22\n    protocol    = &quot;tcp&quot;\n    cidr_blocks = [&quot;0.0.0.0/0&quot;]\n}\negress {\n    from_port   = 0\n    to_port     = 0\n    protocol    = &quot;-1&quot;\n    cidr_blocks = [&quot;0.0.0.0/0&quot;]\n}</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0200","card":"q-terraform-066-auto-scaling-with-cloudwatch-alarms","sec":"terraform-s066","q":"In the Terraform Auto Scaling stack, where does the Auto Scaling group get its subnets?","a":"<p>From the default VPC's subnets data source, through <code>vpc_zone_identifier</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>vpc_zone_identifier = data.aws_subnets.default.ids</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0201","card":"q-terraform-067-auto-scaling-with-cloudwatch-alarms","sec":"terraform-s066","q":"In Terraform, how do you define a step scaling policy that adds one instance?","a":"<p>Use <code>aws_autoscaling_policy</code> with <code>policy_type = \"StepScaling\"</code>, <code>adjustment_type = \"ChangeInCapacity\"</code> and a <code>step_adjustment</code> of <code>1</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>step_adjustment {\n    scaling_adjustment          = 1\n    metric_interval_lower_bound = 0\n}</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0202","card":"q-terraform-067-auto-scaling-with-cloudwatch-alarms","sec":"terraform-s066","q":"In the Terraform Auto Scaling stack, when does the CPU alarm fire?","a":"<p>When average <code>CPUUtilization</code> in <code>AWS/EC2</code> is above 50 over 2 periods of 300 seconds.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>threshold           = 50</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0203","card":"q-terraform-067-auto-scaling-with-cloudwatch-alarms","sec":"terraform-s066","q":"In the Terraform Auto Scaling stack, how does an alarm trigger the scaling policy?","a":"<p><code>alarm_actions</code> holds the policy's ARN, and <code>dimensions</code> targets the Auto Scaling group name.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>dimensions = {\n    AutoScalingGroupName = aws_autoscaling_group.web_asg.name\n}\nalarm_actions = [aws_autoscaling_policy.step_scaling.arn]</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0204","card":"q-terraform-067-auto-scaling-with-cloudwatch-alarms","sec":"terraform-s066","q":"In the Terraform Auto Scaling stack, how is the memory alarm set up?","a":"<p>It watches <code>mem_used_percent</code> in the <code>CWAgent</code> namespace with a threshold of 70.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>metric_name         = &quot;mem_used_percent&quot;\nnamespace           = &quot;CWAgent&quot;\nthreshold           = 70</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0205","card":"q-terraform-068-applying-the-auto-scaling-stack","sec":"terraform-s067","q":"What do you replace before applying the Terraform Auto Scaling stack?","a":"<p>The placeholders <code>&lt;ami-id&gt;</code> and <code>&lt;key-pair-name&gt;</code>. An example AMI is <code>ami-0c55b159cbfafe1f0</code>, Amazon Linux 2 in <code>us-east-1</code>. Save the file as <code>main.tf</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0206","card":"q-terraform-068-applying-the-auto-scaling-stack","sec":"terraform-s067","q":"Which commands apply the Terraform Auto Scaling stack?","a":"<p><code>terraform init</code>, then <code>terraform apply</code>. Confirm with <code>yes</code> when prompted.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>terraform init\nterraform apply</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0207","card":"q-terraform-068-applying-the-auto-scaling-stack","sec":"terraform-s067","q":"What is the result of applying the Terraform Auto Scaling stack?","a":"<p>CPU above 50% adds 1 instance and memory above 70% adds 1 instance. The group scales up to a maximum of 4 instances.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0208","card":"q-terraform-069-s3-bucket-with-public-read-access","sec":"terraform-s068","q":"In Terraform, which three resources make an S3 bucket publicly readable?","a":"<p><code>aws_s3_bucket</code>, <code>aws_s3_bucket_public_access_block</code> and <code>aws_s3_bucket_policy</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0209","card":"q-terraform-069-s3-bucket-with-public-read-access","sec":"terraform-s068","q":"In Terraform, how do you turn off S3 public access blocking for a bucket?","a":"<p>Use <code>aws_s3_bucket_public_access_block</code> and set all four settings to <code>false</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>resource &quot;aws_s3_bucket_public_access_block&quot; &quot;public_bucket&quot; { bucket = aws_s3_bucket.public_bucket.id, block_public_acls = false, block_public_policy = false, ignore_public_acls = false, restrict_public_buckets = false }</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0210","card":"q-terraform-069-s3-bucket-with-public-read-access","sec":"terraform-s068","q":"In Terraform, what does the bucket policy for public read access allow?","a":"<p>It allows everyone (<code>Principal = \"*\"</code>) the action <code>s3:GetObject</code> on all objects in the bucket.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>resource &quot;aws_s3_bucket_policy&quot; &quot;public_read&quot; { bucket = aws_s3_bucket.public_bucket.id, policy = jsonencode({ Version = &quot;2012-10-17&quot;, Statement = [{ Effect = &quot;Allow&quot;, Principal = &quot;*&quot;, Action = &quot;s3:GetObject&quot;, Resource = &quot;${aws_s3_bucket.public_bucket.arn}/*&quot; }] }) }</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0211","card":"q-terraform-070-rds-instance-with-mysql-engine","sec":"terraform-s069","q":"In Terraform, how do you create a MySQL 8.0 RDS instance with 20 GB of storage?","a":"<p>Use <code>aws_db_instance</code> with <code>engine = \"mysql\"</code>, <code>engine_version = \"8.0\"</code> and <code>allocated_storage = 20</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>resource &quot;aws_db_instance&quot; &quot;mysql&quot; { allocated_storage = 20, engine = &quot;mysql&quot;, engine_version = &quot;8.0&quot;, instance_class = &quot;db.t3.micro&quot;, name = &quot;mydb&quot;, username = &quot;admin&quot;, password = &quot;SecurePass123!&quot;, skip_final_snapshot = true, tags = { Name = &quot;MyRDS&quot; } }</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0212","card":"q-terraform-070-rds-instance-with-mysql-engine","sec":"terraform-s069","q":"In Terraform, which other arguments does the MySQL RDS instance set besides engine and storage?","a":"<p><code>instance_class = \"db.t3.micro\"</code>, <code>name = \"mydb\"</code>, <code>username = \"admin\"</code>, a password, <code>skip_final_snapshot = true</code> and a <code>Name</code> tag of <code>MyRDS</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0213","card":"q-terraform-071-s3-bucket-with-glacier-lifecycle-rule","sec":"terraform-s070","q":"In Terraform, which resource moves S3 objects to Glacier?","a":"<p>The <code>aws_s3_bucket_lifecycle_configuration</code> resource, on the bucket.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0214","card":"q-terraform-071-s3-bucket-with-glacier-lifecycle-rule","sec":"terraform-s070","q":"In Terraform, what does the Glacier lifecycle rule set?","a":"<p>A rule with id <code>archive-to-glacier</code>, status <code>Enabled</code>, and a transition after 30 days to the <code>GLACIER</code> storage class.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>resource &quot;aws_s3_bucket_lifecycle_configuration&quot; &quot;lifecycle&quot; { bucket = aws_s3_bucket.lifecycle_bucket.id, rule = { id = &quot;archive-to-glacier&quot;, status = &quot;Enabled&quot;, transition = { days = 30, storage_class = &quot;GLACIER&quot; } } }</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0215","card":"q-terraform-072-dynamodb-table-with-auto-scaling","sec":"terraform-s071","q":"In Terraform, how do you define a provisioned DynamoDB table named <code>MyTable</code> with 5 read and 5 write capacity units?","a":"<p>Use <code>aws_dynamodb_table</code> with <code>billing_mode = \"PROVISIONED\"</code>, <code>read_capacity = 5</code>, <code>write_capacity = 5</code> and <code>hash_key = \"id\"</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>resource &quot;aws_dynamodb_table&quot; &quot;example&quot; { name = &quot;MyTable&quot;, billing_mode = &quot;PROVISIONED&quot;, read_capacity = 5, write_capacity = 5, hash_key = &quot;id&quot;, attribute = { name = &quot;id&quot;, type = &quot;S&quot; } }</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0216","card":"q-terraform-072-dynamodb-table-with-auto-scaling","sec":"terraform-s071","q":"In Terraform, which resource registers a DynamoDB table's read capacity for auto scaling, and what limits does it set?","a":"<p><code>aws_appautoscaling_target</code> with <code>min_capacity = 5</code> and <code>max_capacity = 20</code>. It uses <code>scalable_dimension = \"dynamodb:table:ReadCapacityUnits\"</code> and <code>service_namespace = \"dynamodb\"</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>resource &quot;aws_appautoscaling_target&quot; &quot;read_target&quot; { max_capacity = 20, min_capacity = 5, resource_id = &quot;table/${aws_dynamodb_table.example.name}&quot;, scalable_dimension = &quot;dynamodb:table:ReadCapacityUnits&quot;, service_namespace = &quot;dynamodb&quot; }</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0217","card":"q-terraform-072-dynamodb-table-with-auto-scaling","sec":"terraform-s071","q":"In Terraform, how is a DynamoDB read-capacity scaling policy defined, including its policy type, metric and target value?","a":"<p>Use <code>aws_appautoscaling_policy</code> with <code>policy_type = \"TargetTrackingScaling\"</code>. The predefined metric is <code>DynamoDBReadCapacityUtilization</code> and <code>target_value</code> is <code>70.0</code>. The policy takes <code>resource_id</code>, <code>scalable_dimension</code> and <code>service_namespace</code> from the target.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>resource &quot;aws_appautoscaling_policy&quot; &quot;read_policy&quot; { name = &quot;scale-read&quot;, policy_type = &quot;TargetTrackingScaling&quot;, resource_id = aws_appautoscaling_target.read_target.resource_id, scalable_dimension = aws_appautoscaling_target.read_target.scalable_dimension, service_namespace = aws_appautoscaling_target.read_target.service_namespace, target_tracking_scaling_policy_configuration = { predefined_metric_specification = { predefined_metric_type = &quot;DynamoDBReadCapacityUtilization&quot; }, target_value = 70.0 } }</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0218","card":"q-terraform-073-import-existing-s3-bucket-into-terraform","sec":"terraform-s072","q":"How do you bring an existing S3 bucket under Terraform management without recreating it?","a":"<p>Write a matching <code>aws_s3_bucket</code> resource, then run <code>terraform import</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>resource &quot;aws_s3_bucket&quot; &quot;existing&quot; { bucket = &quot;my-existing-bucket&quot; }</code></pre></div>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>terraform import aws_s3_bucket.existing my-existing-bucket</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0219","card":"q-terraform-073-import-existing-s3-bucket-into-terraform","sec":"terraform-s072","q":"What are the arguments of <code>terraform import</code> when importing an existing S3 bucket named <code>my-existing-bucket</code> into <code>aws_s3_bucket.existing</code>?","a":"<p>The resource address first (<code>aws_s3_bucket.existing</code>), then the bucket name (<code>my-existing-bucket</code>).</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>terraform import aws_s3_bucket.existing my-existing-bucket</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0220","card":"q-terraform-074-manage-existing-rds-instance-without-rec","sec":"terraform-s073","q":"How do you manage an existing RDS instance with Terraform without recreating it?","a":"<p>Define an <code>aws_db_instance</code> resource whose settings match the instance, then import it into state.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>resource &quot;aws_db_instance&quot; &quot;existing_rds&quot; { identifier = &quot;my-existing-db&quot;, engine = &quot;mysql&quot;, instance_class = &quot;db.t3.micro&quot;, allocated_storage = 20, username = &quot;admin&quot;, password = &quot;existingpassword&quot;, skip_final_snapshot = true }</code></pre></div>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>terraform import aws_db_instance.existing_rds my-existing-db</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0221","card":"q-terraform-074-manage-existing-rds-instance-without-rec","sec":"terraform-s073","q":"What <code>terraform import</code> command attaches an existing RDS instance <code>my-existing-db</code> to <code>aws_db_instance.existing_rds</code>?","a":"<p>Run the import with the resource address, then the DB identifier.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>terraform import aws_db_instance.existing_rds my-existing-db</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0222","card":"q-terraform-074-manage-existing-rds-instance-without-rec","sec":"terraform-s073","q":"In Terraform, which attributes does the <code>aws_db_instance</code> resource for an existing MySQL RDS instance set, including its identifier and snapshot behavior?","a":"<p><code>identifier = \"my-existing-db\"</code>, <code>engine = \"mysql\"</code>, <code>instance_class = \"db.t3.micro\"</code>, <code>allocated_storage = 20</code>, <code>username</code>, <code>password</code> and <code>skip_final_snapshot = true</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>resource &quot;aws_db_instance&quot; &quot;existing_rds&quot; { identifier = &quot;my-existing-db&quot;, engine = &quot;mysql&quot;, instance_class = &quot;db.t3.micro&quot;, allocated_storage = 20, username = &quot;admin&quot;, password = &quot;existingpassword&quot;, skip_final_snapshot = true }</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0223","card":"q-terraform-075-s3-bucket-with-server-side-encryption","sec":"terraform-s074","q":"In Terraform, which resource turns on server-side encryption for an S3 bucket, and which <code>sse_algorithm</code> value sets AES-256 encryption?","a":"<p><code>aws_s3_bucket_server_side_encryption_configuration</code> with <code>sse_algorithm = \"AES256\"</code> inside <code>apply_server_side_encryption_by_default</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>resource &quot;aws_s3_bucket_server_side_encryption_configuration&quot; &quot;encryption&quot; { bucket = aws_s3_bucket.bucket.bucket, rule = { apply_server_side_encryption_by_default = { sse_algorithm = &quot;AES256&quot; } } }</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0224","card":"q-terraform-075-s3-bucket-with-server-side-encryption","sec":"terraform-s074","q":"In Terraform, which two extra resources harden an encrypted S3 bucket, and what do they set?","a":"<p><code>aws_s3_bucket_versioning</code> with <code>status = \"Enabled\"</code>, and <code>aws_s3_bucket_public_access_block</code> with <code>block_public_acls</code>, <code>block_public_policy</code>, <code>ignore_public_acls</code> and <code>restrict_public_buckets</code> all <code>true</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>resource &quot;aws_s3_bucket_versioning&quot; &quot;versioning&quot; { bucket = aws_s3_bucket.bucket.bucket, versioning_configuration = { status = &quot;Enabled&quot; } }\nresource &quot;aws_s3_bucket_public_access_block&quot; &quot;block&quot; { bucket = aws_s3_bucket.bucket.bucket, block_public_acls = true, block_public_policy = true, ignore_public_acls = true, restrict_public_buckets = true }</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0225","card":"q-terraform-076-enable-versioning-on-existing-s3-bucket","sec":"terraform-s075","q":"In Terraform, how do you enable versioning on an existing S3 bucket?","a":"<p>Add an <code>aws_s3_bucket_versioning</code> resource that points to the bucket and sets <code>status = \"Enabled\"</code> in <code>versioning_configuration</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>resource &quot;aws_s3_bucket&quot; &quot;existing_bucket&quot; { bucket = &quot;&lt;bucket-name&gt;&quot; }\nresource &quot;aws_s3_bucket_versioning&quot; &quot;versioning&quot; { bucket = aws_s3_bucket.existing_bucket.id, versioning_configuration = { status = &quot;Enabled&quot; } }</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0226","card":"q-terraform-077-resolve-terraform-resource-already-exist","sec":"terraform-s076","q":"How do you fix a Terraform \"resource already exists\" error for an S3 bucket?","a":"<p>Import the existing bucket into state with <code>terraform import</code>, and keep a matching resource block in the configuration.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>resource &quot;aws_s3_bucket&quot; &quot;my_bucket&quot; { bucket = &quot;&lt;bucket-name&gt;&quot; }</code></pre></div>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>terraform import aws_s3_bucket.my_bucket &lt;bucket-name&gt;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0227","card":"q-terraform-078-update-rds-instance-storage-capacity","sec":"terraform-s077","q":"In Terraform, how do you raise the storage of an RDS instance to 50 GB right away?","a":"<p>Set <code>allocated_storage = 50</code> and <code>apply_immediately = true</code> in the <code>aws_db_instance</code> resource.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>resource &quot;aws_db_instance&quot; &quot;example&quot; { identifier = &quot;my-rds-instance&quot;, allocated_storage = 50, instance_class = &quot;db.t3.medium&quot;, engine = &quot;mysql&quot;, username = &quot;admin&quot;, password = &quot;password&quot;, apply_immediately = true }</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0228","card":"q-terraform-079-check-missing-terraform-created-s3-bucke","sec":"terraform-s078","q":"A bucket created through Terraform seems missing. Which three commands check AWS, check state, and re-import it?","a":"<p>Check the bucket in AWS with <code>aws s3 ls</code>, search the state with <code>terraform state list</code>, and import it with <code>terraform import</code> if it is not in state.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>aws s3 ls s3://&lt;bucket-name&gt;\nterraform state list | grep aws_s3_bucket\nterraform import aws_s3_bucket.my_bucket &lt;bucket-name&gt;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0229","card":"q-terraform-079-check-missing-terraform-created-s3-bucke","sec":"terraform-s078","q":"Which command lists S3 buckets tracked in Terraform state?","a":"<p><code>terraform state list</code> piped to <code>grep aws_s3_bucket</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>terraform state list | grep aws_s3_bucket</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0230","card":"q-terraform-080-update-rds-instance-confirm-with-cli","sec":"terraform-s079","q":"In Terraform, how do you change an RDS instance (<code>my-rds-instance</code>) to 30 GB of storage on <code>db.t3.medium</code> with PostgreSQL?","a":"<p>Set <code>allocated_storage = 30</code>, <code>instance_class = \"db.t3.medium\"</code>, <code>engine = \"postgres\"</code> and <code>apply_immediately = true</code> in <code>aws_db_instance</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>resource &quot;aws_db_instance&quot; &quot;example&quot; { identifier = &quot;my-rds-instance&quot;, allocated_storage = 30, instance_class = &quot;db.t3.medium&quot;, engine = &quot;postgres&quot;, username = &quot;admin&quot;, password = &quot;password&quot;, apply_immediately = true }</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0231","card":"q-terraform-080-update-rds-instance-confirm-with-cli","sec":"terraform-s079","q":"After <code>terraform apply</code> changes an RDS instance, which AWS CLI command confirms its status, storage and class?","a":"<p><code>aws rds describe-db-instances</code> with <code>--db-instance-identifier</code> and a <code>--query</code> selecting <code>DBInstanceStatus</code>, <code>AllocatedStorage</code> and <code>DBInstanceClass</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>terraform apply\naws rds describe-db-instances --db-instance-identifier my-rds-instance --query &quot;DBInstances[*].[DBInstanceStatus, AllocatedStorage, DBInstanceClass]&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0232","card":"q-terraform-081-vpc-with-two-private-subnets","sec":"terraform-s080","q":"In Terraform, how do you create a VPC with CIDR <code>10.0.0.0/16</code> and tag it <code>MainVPC</code>?","a":"<p>Use <code>aws_vpc</code> with <code>cidr_block = \"10.0.0.0/16\"</code> and <code>tags = { Name = \"MainVPC\" }</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>resource &quot;aws_vpc&quot; &quot;main&quot; { cidr_block = &quot;10.0.0.0/16&quot;, tags = { Name = &quot;MainVPC&quot; } }</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0233","card":"q-terraform-081-vpc-with-two-private-subnets","sec":"terraform-s080","q":"In Terraform, how do you add two private subnets in <code>us-east-1a</code> and <code>us-east-1b</code> to a VPC?","a":"<p>Create two <code>aws_subnet</code> resources with <code>vpc_id = aws_vpc.main.id</code>: <code>10.0.1.0/24</code> in <code>us-east-1a</code> and <code>10.0.2.0/24</code> in <code>us-east-1b</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>resource &quot;aws_subnet&quot; &quot;private1&quot; { vpc_id = aws_vpc.main.id, cidr_block = &quot;10.0.1.0/24&quot;, availability_zone = &quot;us-east-1a&quot;, tags = { Name = &quot;PrivateSubnet1&quot; } }\nresource &quot;aws_subnet&quot; &quot;private2&quot; { vpc_id = aws_vpc.main.id, cidr_block = &quot;10.0.2.0/24&quot;, availability_zone = &quot;us-east-1b&quot;, tags = { Name = &quot;PrivateSubnet2&quot; } }</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0234","card":"q-terraform-082-module-for-alb-with-target-group","sec":"terraform-s081","q":"In Terraform, how do you call a local <code>./modules/alb</code> module for an ALB, and which inputs does it get?","a":"<p>Use a <code>module \"alb\"</code> block with <code>source = \"./modules/alb\"</code>. Inputs: <code>vpc_id</code>, <code>subnet_ids</code>, <code>alb_name = \"my-alb\"</code> and <code>target_group_name = \"my-target-group\"</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>module &quot;alb&quot; { source = &quot;./modules/alb&quot;, vpc_id = aws_vpc.main.id, subnet_ids = [aws_subnet.private1.id, aws_subnet.private2.id], alb_name = &quot;my-alb&quot;, target_group_name = &quot;my-target-group&quot; }</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0235","card":"q-terraform-082-module-for-alb-with-target-group","sec":"terraform-s081","q":"In Terraform, which resources does the ALB module (<code>modules/alb/main.tf</code>) create?","a":"<p>An <code>aws_lb</code> (not internal, type <code>application</code>) and an <code>aws_lb_target_group</code> on port 80 with protocol HTTP.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>resource &quot;aws_lb&quot; &quot;main&quot; { name = var.alb_name, internal = false, load_balancer_type = &quot;application&quot;, subnets = var.subnet_ids }\nresource &quot;aws_lb_target_group&quot; &quot;main&quot; { name = var.target_group_name, port = 80, protocol = &quot;HTTP&quot;, vpc_id = var.vpc_id }</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0236","card":"q-terraform-082-module-for-alb-with-target-group","sec":"terraform-s081","q":"In Terraform, which input variables does the ALB module declare, and what is the type of <code>subnet_ids</code>?","a":"<p><code>vpc_id</code>, <code>subnet_ids</code>, <code>alb_name</code> and <code>target_group_name</code>. <code>subnet_ids</code> is <code>list(string)</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>variable &quot;vpc_id&quot; {}\nvariable &quot;subnet_ids&quot; { type = list(string) }\nvariable &quot;alb_name&quot; {}\nvariable &quot;target_group_name&quot; {}</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0237","card":"q-terraform-083-security-group-with-ssh-http-inbound-rul","sec":"terraform-s082","q":"In Terraform, how do you build a security group that allows SSH and HTTP inbound and all outbound traffic?","a":"<p>Use <code>aws_security_group</code> with <code>ingress</code> rules for port 22 and port 80 (<code>tcp</code>, <code>0.0.0.0/0</code>) and an <code>egress</code> rule with <code>from_port = 0</code>, <code>to_port = 0</code>, <code>protocol = \"-1\"</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>resource &quot;aws_security_group&quot; &quot;example&quot; { name = &quot;allow_ssh_http&quot;, vpc_id = aws_vpc.main.id, ingress = [{ from_port = 22, to_port = 22, protocol = &quot;tcp&quot;, cidr_blocks = [&quot;0.0.0.0/0&quot;] }, { from_port = 80, to_port = 80, protocol = &quot;tcp&quot;, cidr_blocks = [&quot;0.0.0.0/0&quot;] }], egress = [{ from_port = 0, to_port = 0, protocol = &quot;-1&quot;, cidr_blocks = [&quot;0.0.0.0/0&quot;] }] }</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0238","card":"q-terraform-084-cloudfront-distribution-for-s3-bucket","sec":"terraform-s083","q":"In Terraform, how do you point a CloudFront distribution at an S3 bucket origin?","a":"<p>Set <code>origin</code> with <code>domain_name = aws_s3_bucket.bucket.bucket_regional_domain_name</code> and <code>origin_id = \"S3Origin\"</code>, then reference that id in <code>target_origin_id</code> of <code>default_cache_behavior</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>resource &quot;aws_cloudfront_distribution&quot; &quot;s3_distribution&quot; { origin = { domain_name = aws_s3_bucket.bucket.bucket_regional_domain_name, origin_id = &quot;S3Origin&quot; }, enabled = true, is_ipv6_enabled = true, default_root_object = &quot;index.html&quot;, default_cache_behavior = { allowed_methods = [&quot;GET&quot;, &quot;HEAD&quot;], cached_methods = [&quot;GET&quot;, &quot;HEAD&quot;], target_origin_id = &quot;S3Origin&quot;, forwarded_values = { query_string = false, cookies = { forward = &quot;none&quot; } }, viewer_protocol_policy = &quot;redirect-to-https&quot; }, restrictions = { geo_restriction = { restriction_type = &quot;none&quot; } }, viewer_certificate = { cloudfront_default_certificate = true } }</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0239","card":"q-terraform-084-cloudfront-distribution-for-s3-bucket","sec":"terraform-s083","q":"In Terraform, which CloudFront settings serve <code>index.html</code> and redirect viewers to HTTPS?","a":"<p><code>default_root_object = \"index.html\"</code> and <code>viewer_protocol_policy = \"redirect-to-https\"</code> in <code>default_cache_behavior</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>resource &quot;aws_cloudfront_distribution&quot; &quot;s3_distribution&quot; { origin = { domain_name = aws_s3_bucket.bucket.bucket_regional_domain_name, origin_id = &quot;S3Origin&quot; }, enabled = true, is_ipv6_enabled = true, default_root_object = &quot;index.html&quot;, default_cache_behavior = { allowed_methods = [&quot;GET&quot;, &quot;HEAD&quot;], cached_methods = [&quot;GET&quot;, &quot;HEAD&quot;], target_origin_id = &quot;S3Origin&quot;, forwarded_values = { query_string = false, cookies = { forward = &quot;none&quot; } }, viewer_protocol_policy = &quot;redirect-to-https&quot; }, restrictions = { geo_restriction = { restriction_type = &quot;none&quot; } }, viewer_certificate = { cloudfront_default_certificate = true } }</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0240","card":"q-terraform-084-cloudfront-distribution-for-s3-bucket","sec":"terraform-s083","q":"In Terraform, which CloudFront settings control allowed methods, geo restriction and the certificate?","a":"<p><code>allowed_methods</code> and <code>cached_methods</code> are <code>[\"GET\", \"HEAD\"]</code>. <code>geo_restriction</code> has <code>restriction_type = \"none\"</code>. <code>viewer_certificate</code> uses <code>cloudfront_default_certificate = true</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>resource &quot;aws_cloudfront_distribution&quot; &quot;s3_distribution&quot; { origin = { domain_name = aws_s3_bucket.bucket.bucket_regional_domain_name, origin_id = &quot;S3Origin&quot; }, enabled = true, is_ipv6_enabled = true, default_root_object = &quot;index.html&quot;, default_cache_behavior = { allowed_methods = [&quot;GET&quot;, &quot;HEAD&quot;], cached_methods = [&quot;GET&quot;, &quot;HEAD&quot;], target_origin_id = &quot;S3Origin&quot;, forwarded_values = { query_string = false, cookies = { forward = &quot;none&quot; } }, viewer_protocol_policy = &quot;redirect-to-https&quot; }, restrictions = { geo_restriction = { restriction_type = &quot;none&quot; } }, viewer_certificate = { cloudfront_default_certificate = true } }</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0241","card":"q-terraform-085-nat-gateway-in-a-vpc","sec":"terraform-s084","q":"In Terraform, which resources do you need for a NAT Gateway in a VPC?","a":"<p>A VPC, a public subnet, an internet gateway, an Elastic IP (<code>aws_eip</code>) and the <code>aws_nat_gateway</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>resource &quot;aws_vpc&quot; &quot;main&quot; { cidr_block = &quot;10.0.0.0/16&quot; }\nresource &quot;aws_subnet&quot; &quot;public&quot; { vpc_id = aws_vpc.main.id, cidr_block = &quot;10.0.1.0/24&quot; }\nresource &quot;aws_internet_gateway&quot; &quot;igw&quot; { vpc_id = aws_vpc.main.id }\nresource &quot;aws_eip&quot; &quot;nat_eip&quot; { vpc = true }\nresource &quot;aws_nat_gateway&quot; &quot;nat&quot; { allocation_id = aws_eip.nat_eip.id, subnet_id = aws_subnet.public.id, depends_on = [aws_internet_gateway.igw] }</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0242","card":"q-terraform-085-nat-gateway-in-a-vpc","sec":"terraform-s084","q":"In Terraform, how does <code>aws_nat_gateway</code> get its address and subnet, and why does it have <code>depends_on</code>?","a":"<p>It takes <code>allocation_id</code> from the Elastic IP and <code>subnet_id</code> from the public subnet. <code>depends_on = [aws_internet_gateway.igw]</code> makes Terraform create the internet gateway first.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>resource &quot;aws_nat_gateway&quot; &quot;nat&quot; { allocation_id = aws_eip.nat_eip.id, subnet_id = aws_subnet.public.id, depends_on = [aws_internet_gateway.igw] }</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0243","card":"q-terraform-086-ec2-instance-behind-a-load-balancer","sec":"terraform-s085","q":"In Terraform, which resources put an EC2 instance behind an application load balancer?","a":"<p>A VPC and public subnet, a security group for the ALB, <code>aws_lb</code>, <code>aws_lb_target_group</code>, <code>aws_lb_listener</code>, <code>aws_instance</code> and <code>aws_lb_target_group_attachment</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>resource &quot;aws_vpc&quot; &quot;main&quot; { cidr_block = &quot;10.0.0.0/16&quot; }\nresource &quot;aws_subnet&quot; &quot;public&quot; { vpc_id = aws_vpc.main.id, cidr_block = &quot;10.0.1.0/24&quot; }\nresource &quot;aws_security_group&quot; &quot;alb_sg&quot; { vpc_id = aws_vpc.main.id, ingress = { from_port = 80, to_port = 80, protocol = &quot;tcp&quot;, cidr_blocks = [&quot;0.0.0.0/0&quot;] }, egress = { from_port = 0, to_port = 0, protocol = &quot;-1&quot;, cidr_blocks = [&quot;0.0.0.0/0&quot;] } }\nresource &quot;aws_lb&quot; &quot;example&quot; { name = &quot;my-alb&quot;, internal = false, load_balancer_type = &quot;application&quot;, security_groups = [aws_security_group.alb_sg.id], subnets = [aws_subnet.public.id] }\nresource &quot;aws_lb_target_group&quot; &quot;example&quot; { name = &quot;my-tg&quot;, port = 80, protocol = &quot;HTTP&quot;, vpc_id = aws_vpc.main.id }\nresource &quot;aws_lb_listener&quot; &quot;example&quot; { load_balancer_arn = aws_lb.example.arn, port = 80, protocol = &quot;HTTP&quot;, default_action = { type = &quot;forward&quot;, target_group_arn = aws_lb_target_group.example.arn } }\nresource &quot;aws_instance&quot; &quot;example&quot; { ami = &quot;ami-0c55b159cbfafe1f0&quot;, instance_type = &quot;t2.micro&quot;, subnet_id = aws_subnet.public.id, security_groups = [aws_security_group.alb_sg.name] }\nresource &quot;aws_lb_target_group_attachment&quot; &quot;example&quot; { target_group_arn = aws_lb_target_group.example.arn, target_id = aws_instance.example.id, port = 80 }</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0244","card":"q-terraform-086-ec2-instance-behind-a-load-balancer","sec":"terraform-s085","q":"In Terraform, how does an <code>aws_lb_listener</code> on port 80 send traffic to a target group?","a":"<p><code>default_action</code> has <code>type = \"forward\"</code> and <code>target_group_arn</code> of the target group.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>resource &quot;aws_lb_listener&quot; &quot;example&quot; { load_balancer_arn = aws_lb.example.arn, port = 80, protocol = &quot;HTTP&quot;, default_action = { type = &quot;forward&quot;, target_group_arn = aws_lb_target_group.example.arn } }</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0245","card":"q-terraform-086-ec2-instance-behind-a-load-balancer","sec":"terraform-s085","q":"In Terraform, how is an EC2 instance registered with a load balancer target group?","a":"<p><code>aws_lb_target_group_attachment</code> with <code>target_group_arn</code>, <code>target_id = aws_instance.example.id</code> and <code>port = 80</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>resource &quot;aws_lb_target_group_attachment&quot; &quot;example&quot; { target_group_arn = aws_lb_target_group.example.arn, target_id = aws_instance.example.id, port = 80 }</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0246","card":"q-terraform-087-route-53-record-for-alb","sec":"terraform-s086","q":"In Terraform, how do you point <code>www.example.com</code> at an ALB with Route 53?","a":"<p>Create an <code>aws_route53_zone</code> for <code>example.com</code>, then an <code>aws_route53_record</code> of <code>type = \"A\"</code> with an <code>alias</code> block.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>resource &quot;aws_route53_zone&quot; &quot;example&quot; { name = &quot;example.com&quot; }\nresource &quot;aws_route53_record&quot; &quot;www&quot; { zone_id = aws_route53_zone.example.zone_id, name = &quot;www.example.com&quot;, type = &quot;A&quot;, alias = { name = aws_lb.example.dns_name, zone_id = aws_lb.example.zone_id, evaluate_target_health = true } }</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0247","card":"q-terraform-087-route-53-record-for-alb","sec":"terraform-s086","q":"In Terraform, which values go into the <code>alias</code> block of a Route 53 record for an ALB?","a":"<p><code>name</code> is the ALB <code>dns_name</code>, <code>zone_id</code> is the ALB <code>zone_id</code>, and <code>evaluate_target_health = true</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>resource &quot;aws_route53_record&quot; &quot;www&quot; { zone_id = aws_route53_zone.example.zone_id, name = &quot;www.example.com&quot;, type = &quot;A&quot;, alias = { name = aws_lb.example.dns_name, zone_id = aws_lb.example.zone_id, evaluate_target_health = true } }</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0248","card":"q-terraform-088-vpc-peering-connection-between-two-vpcs","sec":"terraform-s087","q":"In Terraform, how do you create a peering connection between two VPCs?","a":"<p>Use <code>aws_vpc_peering_connection</code> with <code>vpc_id</code>, <code>peer_vpc_id</code> and <code>auto_accept = true</code>. The VPCs are <code>10.0.0.0/16</code> and <code>10.1.0.0/16</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>resource &quot;aws_vpc&quot; &quot;vpc_a&quot; { cidr_block = &quot;10.0.0.0/16&quot; }\nresource &quot;aws_vpc&quot; &quot;vpc_b&quot; { cidr_block = &quot;10.1.0.0/16&quot; }\nresource &quot;aws_vpc_peering_connection&quot; &quot;peer&quot; { vpc_id = aws_vpc.vpc_a.id, peer_vpc_id = aws_vpc.vpc_b.id, auto_accept = true }\nresource &quot;aws_route&quot; &quot;vpc_a_route&quot; { route_table_id = aws_vpc.vpc_a.main_route_table_id, destination_cidr_block = aws_vpc.vpc_b.cidr_block, vpc_peering_connection_id = aws_vpc_peering_connection.peer.id }\nresource &quot;aws_route&quot; &quot;vpc_b_route&quot; { route_table_id = aws_vpc.vpc_b.main_route_table_id, destination_cidr_block = aws_vpc.vpc_a.cidr_block, vpc_peering_connection_id = aws_vpc_peering_connection.peer.id }</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0249","card":"q-terraform-088-vpc-peering-connection-between-two-vpcs","sec":"terraform-s087","q":"In Terraform, what routes must you add after creating a VPC peering connection?","a":"<p>An <code>aws_route</code> in each VPC main route table, with the other VPC CIDR as <code>destination_cidr_block</code> and <code>vpc_peering_connection_id</code> of the peering connection.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>resource &quot;aws_route&quot; &quot;vpc_a_route&quot; { route_table_id = aws_vpc.vpc_a.main_route_table_id, destination_cidr_block = aws_vpc.vpc_b.cidr_block, vpc_peering_connection_id = aws_vpc_peering_connection.peer.id }\nresource &quot;aws_route&quot; &quot;vpc_b_route&quot; { route_table_id = aws_vpc.vpc_b.main_route_table_id, destination_cidr_block = aws_vpc.vpc_a.cidr_block, vpc_peering_connection_id = aws_vpc_peering_connection.peer.id }</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0250","card":"q-terraform-089-add-new-subnet-to-existing-vpc","sec":"terraform-s088","q":"In Terraform, how do you add a subnet <code>10.0.3.0/24</code> in <code>us-east-1c</code> to an existing VPC?","a":"<p>Add an <code>aws_subnet</code> with <code>vpc_id = aws_vpc.existing_vpc.id</code>, <code>cidr_block = \"10.0.3.0/24\"</code> and <code>availability_zone = \"us-east-1c\"</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>resource &quot;aws_vpc&quot; &quot;existing_vpc&quot; { cidr_block = &quot;10.0.0.0/16&quot; }\nresource &quot;aws_subnet&quot; &quot;new_subnet&quot; { vpc_id = aws_vpc.existing_vpc.id, cidr_block = &quot;10.0.3.0/24&quot;, availability_zone = &quot;us-east-1c&quot; }</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0251","card":"q-terraform-090-fix-terraform-alb-not-routing-traffic","sec":"terraform-s089","q":"In Terraform, which resource makes an ALB forward traffic to a target group?","a":"<p>An <code>aws_lb_listener</code> on port 80 with <code>default_action</code> of <code>type = \"forward\"</code> and the target group ARN.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>resource &quot;aws_lb_listener&quot; &quot;listener&quot; { load_balancer_arn = aws_lb.example.arn, port = 80, protocol = &quot;HTTP&quot;, default_action = { type = &quot;forward&quot;, target_group_arn = aws_lb_target_group.tg.arn } }</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0252","card":"q-terraform-090-fix-terraform-alb-not-routing-traffic","sec":"terraform-s089","q":"In Terraform, which <code>aws_lb</code> arguments make an internet-facing application load balancer with a security group and two public subnets?","a":"<p><code>internal = false</code>, <code>load_balancer_type = \"application\"</code>, a security group, and two public subnets (<code>public1</code> and <code>public2</code>).</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>resource &quot;aws_lb&quot; &quot;example&quot; { name = &quot;my-alb&quot;, internal = false, load_balancer_type = &quot;application&quot;, security_groups = [aws_security_group.alb.id], subnets = [aws_subnet.public1.id, aws_subnet.public2.id] }</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0253","card":"q-terraform-091-update-security-group-with-new-inbound-r","sec":"terraform-s090","q":"In Terraform, how do you add an inbound HTTPS rule to an existing security group?","a":"<p>Add an <code>aws_security_group_rule</code> with <code>type = \"ingress\"</code>, port 443, <code>protocol = \"tcp\"</code>, <code>cidr_blocks = [\"0.0.0.0/0\"]</code> and <code>security_group_id</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>resource &quot;aws_security_group&quot; &quot;example&quot; { name = &quot;my-sg&quot;, vpc_id = aws_vpc.main.id }\nresource &quot;aws_security_group_rule&quot; &quot;new_rule&quot; { type = &quot;ingress&quot;, from_port = 443, to_port = 443, protocol = &quot;tcp&quot;, cidr_blocks = [&quot;0.0.0.0/0&quot;], security_group_id = aws_security_group.example.id }</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0254","card":"q-terraform-092-ec2-instance-with-specific-key-pair","sec":"terraform-s091","q":"In Terraform, how do you launch an EC2 instance with a specific key pair?","a":"<p>Set <code>key_name = \"my-key-pair\"</code> in the <code>aws_instance</code> resource.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>resource &quot;aws_instance&quot; &quot;example&quot; { ami = &quot;ami-0c55b159cbfafe1f0&quot;, instance_type = &quot;t2.micro&quot;, key_name = &quot;my-key-pair&quot;, tags = { Name = &quot;MyEC2Instance&quot; } }</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0255","card":"q-terraform-093-auto-scaling-group-with-launch-template","sec":"terraform-s092","q":"In Terraform, how do you create a launch template for <code>t2.micro</code> instances?","a":"<p>Use <code>aws_launch_template</code> with <code>name_prefix = \"example-\"</code>, <code>image_id</code> and <code>instance_type = \"t2.micro\"</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>resource &quot;aws_launch_template&quot; &quot;example&quot; { name_prefix = &quot;example-&quot;, image_id = &quot;ami-0c55b159cbfafe1f0&quot;, instance_type = &quot;t2.micro&quot; }</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0256","card":"q-terraform-093-auto-scaling-group-with-launch-template","sec":"terraform-s092","q":"In Terraform, how does an Auto Scaling group use a launch template and which sizes does it set?","a":"<p><code>launch_template</code> takes the template <code>id</code> with <code>version = \"$Latest\"</code>. Sizes: <code>desired_capacity = 2</code>, <code>max_size = 3</code>, <code>min_size = 1</code>. <code>vpc_zone_identifier</code> lists two private subnets.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>resource &quot;aws_autoscaling_group&quot; &quot;example&quot; { desired_capacity = 2, max_size = 3, min_size = 1, vpc_zone_identifier = [aws_subnet.private1.id, aws_subnet.private2.id], launch_template = { id = aws_launch_template.example.id, version = &quot;$Latest&quot; } }</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0257","card":"q-terraform-094-cloudwatch-monitoring-on-ec2-instance","sec":"terraform-s093","q":"In Terraform, how do you turn on monitoring for an EC2 instance?","a":"<p>Set <code>monitoring = true</code> in <code>aws_instance</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>resource &quot;aws_instance&quot; &quot;monitored&quot; { ami = &quot;ami-0c55b159cbfafe1f0&quot;, instance_type = &quot;t2.micro&quot;, monitoring = true, tags = { Name = &quot;MonitoredEC2&quot; } }</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0258","card":"q-terraform-094-cloudwatch-monitoring-on-ec2-instance","sec":"terraform-s093","q":"In Terraform, how do you alarm when an EC2 instance CPU stays above 80 percent?","a":"<p>Use <code>aws_cloudwatch_metric_alarm</code> with <code>metric_name = \"CPUUtilization\"</code>, <code>namespace = \"AWS/EC2\"</code>, <code>statistic = \"Average\"</code>, <code>period = 300</code>, <code>evaluation_periods = 2</code>, <code>comparison_operator = \"GreaterThanThreshold\"</code>, <code>threshold = 80</code> and the instance in <code>dimensions</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>resource &quot;aws_cloudwatch_metric_alarm&quot; &quot;cpu&quot; { alarm_name = &quot;high-cpu-usage&quot;, comparison_operator = &quot;GreaterThanThreshold&quot;, evaluation_periods = 2, metric_name = &quot;CPUUtilization&quot;, namespace = &quot;AWS/EC2&quot;, period = 300, statistic = &quot;Average&quot;, threshold = 80, dimensions = { InstanceId = aws_instance.monitored.id } }</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0259","card":"q-terraform-095-eks-cluster-with-single-node-group","sec":"terraform-s094","q":"In Terraform, how do you create an EKS cluster?","a":"<p>Use <code>aws_eks_cluster</code> with a <code>name</code>, a <code>role_arn</code> and <code>vpc_config</code> holding <code>subnet_ids</code> of two private subnets.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>resource &quot;aws_eks_cluster&quot; &quot;example&quot; { name = &quot;my-eks-cluster&quot;, role_arn = aws_iam_role.eks_role.arn, vpc_config = { subnet_ids = [aws_subnet.private1.id, aws_subnet.private2.id] } }</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0260","card":"q-terraform-095-eks-cluster-with-single-node-group","sec":"terraform-s094","q":"In Terraform, how do you add a node group with one desired node to an EKS cluster?","a":"<p>Use <code>aws_eks_node_group</code> with <code>cluster_name</code>, <code>node_group_name</code>, <code>node_role_arn</code>, <code>subnet_ids</code> and <code>scaling_config</code> of <code>desired_size = 1</code>, <code>max_size = 2</code>, <code>min_size = 1</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>resource &quot;aws_eks_node_group&quot; &quot;example&quot; { cluster_name = aws_eks_cluster.example.name, node_group_name = &quot;my-node-group&quot;, node_role_arn = aws_iam_role.node_role.arn, subnet_ids = [aws_subnet.private1.id, aws_subnet.private2.id], scaling_config = { desired_size = 1, max_size = 2, min_size = 1 } }</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0261","card":"q-terraform-095-eks-cluster-with-single-node-group","sec":"terraform-s094","q":"In Terraform, which service principals do the EKS cluster role and the node role trust?","a":"<p>The cluster role trusts <code>eks.amazonaws.com</code>. The node role trusts <code>ec2.amazonaws.com</code>. Both use the action <code>sts:AssumeRole</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>resource &quot;aws_iam_role&quot; &quot;eks_role&quot; { name = &quot;eks-role&quot;, assume_role_policy = jsonencode({ Version = &quot;2012-10-17&quot;, Statement = [{ Action = &quot;sts:AssumeRole&quot;, Effect = &quot;Allow&quot;, Principal = { Service = &quot;eks.amazonaws.com&quot; } }] }) }\nresource &quot;aws_iam_role&quot; &quot;node_role&quot; { name = &quot;eks-node-role&quot;, assume_role_policy = jsonencode({ Version = &quot;2012-10-17&quot;, Statement = [{ Action = &quot;sts:AssumeRole&quot;, Effect = &quot;Allow&quot;, Principal = { Service = &quot;ec2.amazonaws.com&quot; } }] }) }</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0262","card":"q-terraform-096-iam-role-with-s3-full-access","sec":"terraform-s095","q":"In Terraform, how do you give an EC2-assumable IAM role full S3 access?","a":"<p>Create an <code>aws_iam_role</code> that trusts <code>ec2.amazonaws.com</code>, then attach the managed policy with <code>aws_iam_role_policy_attachment</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>resource &quot;aws_iam_role&quot; &quot;s3_full_access&quot; { name = &quot;s3-full-access-role&quot;, assume_role_policy = jsonencode({ Version = &quot;2012-10-17&quot;, Statement = [{ Action = &quot;sts:AssumeRole&quot;, Effect = &quot;Allow&quot;, Principal = { Service = &quot;ec2.amazonaws.com&quot; } }] }) }\nresource &quot;aws_iam_role_policy_attachment&quot; &quot;s3_full_access&quot; { role = aws_iam_role.s3_full_access.name, policy_arn = &quot;arn:aws:iam::aws:policy/AmazonS3FullAccess&quot; }</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0263","card":"q-terraform-096-iam-role-with-s3-full-access","sec":"terraform-s095","q":"In Terraform, which managed policy ARN grants a role full S3 access?","a":"<p><code>arn:aws:iam::aws:policy/AmazonS3FullAccess</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>resource &quot;aws_iam_role_policy_attachment&quot; &quot;s3_full_access&quot; { role = aws_iam_role.s3_full_access.name, policy_arn = &quot;arn:aws:iam::aws:policy/AmazonS3FullAccess&quot; }</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0264","card":"q-terraform-097-lambda-function-triggered-by-s3-event","sec":"terraform-s096","q":"In Terraform, which resources does a Lambda function triggered by an S3 event need?","a":"<p>An S3 bucket, a Lambda execution role with a policy attachment, <code>aws_lambda_function</code>, <code>aws_s3_bucket_notification</code> and <code>aws_lambda_permission</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>resource &quot;aws_s3_bucket&quot; &quot;bucket&quot; { bucket = &quot;my-lambda-trigger-bucket&quot; }\nresource &quot;aws_iam_role&quot; &quot;lambda_role&quot; { name = &quot;lambda_execution_role&quot;, assume_role_policy = jsonencode({ Version = &quot;2012-10-17&quot;, Statement = [{ Action = &quot;sts:AssumeRole&quot;, Effect = &quot;Allow&quot;, Principal = { Service = &quot;lambda.amazonaws.com&quot; } }] }) }\nresource &quot;aws_iam_role_policy_attachment&quot; &quot;lambda_policy&quot; { role = aws_iam_role.lambda_role.name, policy_arn = &quot;arn:aws:iam::aws:policy/service-role/AWSLambdaBasicExecutionRole&quot; }\nresource &quot;aws_lambda_function&quot; &quot;example&quot; { filename = &quot;lambda_function.zip&quot;, function_name = &quot;s3_trigger_lambda&quot;, role = aws_iam_role.lambda_role.arn, handler = &quot;index.handler&quot;, runtime = &quot;nodejs18.x&quot; }\nresource &quot;aws_s3_bucket_notification&quot; &quot;bucket_notification&quot; { bucket = aws_s3_bucket.bucket.id, lambda_function = { lambda_function_arn = aws_lambda_function.example.arn, events = [&quot;s3:ObjectCreated:*&quot;] } }\nresource &quot;aws_lambda_permission&quot; &quot;allow_s3&quot; { statement_id = &quot;AllowS3Invoke&quot;, action = &quot;lambda:InvokeFunction&quot;, function_name = aws_lambda_function.example.function_name, principal = &quot;s3.amazonaws.com&quot;, source_arn = aws_s3_bucket.bucket.arn }</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0265","card":"q-terraform-097-lambda-function-triggered-by-s3-event","sec":"terraform-s096","q":"In Terraform, which managed policy and trusted service give a Lambda execution role basic permissions?","a":"<p>The role trusts <code>lambda.amazonaws.com</code>. It attaches <code>arn:aws:iam::aws:policy/service-role/AWSLambdaBasicExecutionRole</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>resource &quot;aws_iam_role&quot; &quot;lambda_role&quot; { name = &quot;lambda_execution_role&quot;, assume_role_policy = jsonencode({ Version = &quot;2012-10-17&quot;, Statement = [{ Action = &quot;sts:AssumeRole&quot;, Effect = &quot;Allow&quot;, Principal = { Service = &quot;lambda.amazonaws.com&quot; } }] }) }\nresource &quot;aws_iam_role_policy_attachment&quot; &quot;lambda_policy&quot; { role = aws_iam_role.lambda_role.name, policy_arn = &quot;arn:aws:iam::aws:policy/service-role/AWSLambdaBasicExecutionRole&quot; }</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0266","card":"q-terraform-097-lambda-function-triggered-by-s3-event","sec":"terraform-s096","q":"In Terraform, how do you let S3 call a Lambda function?","a":"<p>Add <code>aws_lambda_permission</code> with <code>action = \"lambda:InvokeFunction\"</code>, <code>principal = \"s3.amazonaws.com\"</code> and <code>source_arn</code> of the bucket.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>resource &quot;aws_lambda_permission&quot; &quot;allow_s3&quot; { statement_id = &quot;AllowS3Invoke&quot;, action = &quot;lambda:InvokeFunction&quot;, function_name = aws_lambda_function.example.function_name, principal = &quot;s3.amazonaws.com&quot;, source_arn = aws_s3_bucket.bucket.arn }</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0267","card":"q-terraform-097-lambda-function-triggered-by-s3-event","sec":"terraform-s096","q":"In Terraform, how does <code>aws_s3_bucket_notification</code> trigger a Lambda function on object creation?","a":"<p>It sets <code>lambda_function_arn</code> and <code>events = [\"s3:ObjectCreated:*\"]</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>resource &quot;aws_s3_bucket_notification&quot; &quot;bucket_notification&quot; { bucket = aws_s3_bucket.bucket.id, lambda_function = { lambda_function_arn = aws_lambda_function.example.arn, events = [&quot;s3:ObjectCreated:*&quot;] } }</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0268","card":"q-terraform-098-ecs-cluster-with-fargate-task-definition","sec":"terraform-s097","q":"In Terraform, how do you create an ECS cluster?","a":"<p>Use <code>aws_ecs_cluster</code> with a <code>name</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>resource &quot;aws_ecs_cluster&quot; &quot;example&quot; { name = &quot;my-ecs-cluster&quot; }</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0269","card":"q-terraform-098-ecs-cluster-with-fargate-task-definition","sec":"terraform-s097","q":"In Terraform, which role and policy does an ECS Fargate task execution role use?","a":"<p>The role trusts <code>ecs-tasks.amazonaws.com</code>. It attaches <code>arn:aws:iam::aws:policy/service-role/AmazonECSTaskExecutionRolePolicy</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>resource &quot;aws_iam_role&quot; &quot;ecs_task_execution_role&quot; { name = &quot;ecsTaskExecutionRole&quot;, assume_role_policy = jsonencode({ Version = &quot;2012-10-17&quot;, Statement = [{ Action = &quot;sts:AssumeRole&quot;, Effect = &quot;Allow&quot;, Principal = { Service = &quot;ecs-tasks.amazonaws.com&quot; } }] }) }\nresource &quot;aws_iam_role_policy_attachment&quot; &quot;ecs_task_execution_policy&quot; { role = aws_iam_role.ecs_task_execution_role.name, policy_arn = &quot;arn:aws:iam::aws:policy/service-role/AmazonECSTaskExecutionRolePolicy&quot; }</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0270","card":"q-terraform-098-ecs-cluster-with-fargate-task-definition","sec":"terraform-s097","q":"In Terraform, which settings make an ECS task definition Fargate-compatible?","a":"<p><code>network_mode = \"awsvpc\"</code>, <code>requires_compatibilities = [\"FARGATE\"]</code>, <code>cpu = \"256\"</code> and <code>memory = \"512\"</code>, plus <code>execution_role_arn</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>resource &quot;aws_ecs_task_definition&quot; &quot;example&quot; { family = &quot;my-fargate-task&quot;, network_mode = &quot;awsvpc&quot;, requires_compatibilities = [&quot;FARGATE&quot;], cpu = &quot;256&quot;, memory = &quot;512&quot;, execution_role_arn = aws_iam_role.ecs_task_execution_role.arn, container_definitions = jsonencode([{ name = &quot;my-container&quot;, image = &quot;amazon/amazon-ecs-sample&quot;, portMappings = [{ containerPort = 80, hostPort = 80 }]}]) }</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0271","card":"q-terraform-098-ecs-cluster-with-fargate-task-definition","sec":"terraform-s097","q":"In Terraform, how does an ECS service run a task on Fargate?","a":"<p>Use <code>aws_ecs_service</code> with <code>launch_type = \"FARGATE\"</code>, <code>desired_count = 1</code>, the <code>cluster</code>, the <code>task_definition</code> and a <code>network_configuration</code> with subnets and security groups.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>resource &quot;aws_ecs_service&quot; &quot;example&quot; { name = &quot;my-service&quot;, cluster = aws_ecs_cluster.example.id, task_definition = aws_ecs_task_definition.example.arn, launch_type = &quot;FARGATE&quot;, desired_count = 1, network_configuration = { subnets = [aws_subnet.public.id], security_groups = [aws_security_group.example.id] } }</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0272","card":"q-terraform-099-sns-topic-with-email-subscription","sec":"terraform-s098","q":"In Terraform, how do you create an SNS topic?","a":"<p>Use <code>aws_sns_topic</code> with a <code>name</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>resource &quot;aws_sns_topic&quot; &quot;example&quot; { name = &quot;my-sns-topic&quot; }</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0273","card":"q-terraform-099-sns-topic-with-email-subscription","sec":"terraform-s098","q":"In Terraform, how do you subscribe an email address to an SNS topic?","a":"<p>Use <code>aws_sns_topic_subscription</code> with <code>topic_arn</code>, <code>protocol = \"email\"</code> and <code>endpoint</code> set to the address.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>resource &quot;aws_sns_topic_subscription&quot; &quot;email&quot; { topic_arn = aws_sns_topic.example.arn, protocol = &quot;email&quot;, endpoint = &quot;user@example.com&quot; }</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0274","card":"q-terraform-100-cloudwatch-alarm-for-ec2-cpu-utilization","sec":"terraform-s099","q":"In Terraform, how do you create a CloudWatch alarm on EC2 CPU utilization?","a":"<p>Use <code>aws_cloudwatch_metric_alarm</code> with <code>metric_name = \"CPUUtilization\"</code>, <code>namespace = \"AWS/EC2\"</code> and <code>InstanceId</code> in <code>dimensions</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>resource &quot;aws_cloudwatch_metric_alarm&quot; &quot;cpu_alarm&quot; { alarm_name = &quot;ec2-cpu-utilization&quot;, comparison_operator = &quot;GreaterThanThreshold&quot;, evaluation_periods = &quot;2&quot;, metric_name = &quot;CPUUtilization&quot;, namespace = &quot;AWS/EC2&quot;, period = &quot;300&quot;, statistic = &quot;Average&quot;, threshold = &quot;80&quot;, dimensions = { InstanceId = aws_instance.example.id } }</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0275","card":"q-terraform-100-cloudwatch-alarm-for-ec2-cpu-utilization","sec":"terraform-s099","q":"In Terraform, which threshold, period and evaluation settings does the EC2 CPU alarm use?","a":"<p><code>threshold = \"80\"</code>, <code>period = \"300\"</code>, <code>evaluation_periods = \"2\"</code>, <code>statistic = \"Average\"</code> and <code>comparison_operator = \"GreaterThanThreshold\"</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>resource &quot;aws_cloudwatch_metric_alarm&quot; &quot;cpu_alarm&quot; { alarm_name = &quot;ec2-cpu-utilization&quot;, comparison_operator = &quot;GreaterThanThreshold&quot;, evaluation_periods = &quot;2&quot;, metric_name = &quot;CPUUtilization&quot;, namespace = &quot;AWS/EC2&quot;, period = &quot;300&quot;, statistic = &quot;Average&quot;, threshold = &quot;80&quot;, dimensions = { InstanceId = aws_instance.example.id } }</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0276","card":"q-terraform-101-elastic-beanstalk-application","sec":"terraform-s100","q":"In Terraform, how do you create an Elastic Beanstalk application and environment?","a":"<p>Use <code>aws_elastic_beanstalk_application</code>, then <code>aws_elastic_beanstalk_environment</code> that references the application name and sets <code>solution_stack_name</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>resource &quot;aws_elastic_beanstalk_application&quot; &quot;app&quot; { name = &quot;my-eb-app&quot; }\nresource &quot;aws_elastic_beanstalk_environment&quot; &quot;env&quot; { name = &quot;my-eb-env&quot;, application = aws_elastic_beanstalk_application.app.name, solution_stack_name = &quot;64bit Amazon Linux 2 v3.3.13 running Python 3.8&quot;, setting = { namespace = &quot;aws:autoscaling:launchconfiguration&quot;, name = &quot;InstanceType&quot;, value = &quot;t2.micro&quot; } }</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0277","card":"q-terraform-101-elastic-beanstalk-application","sec":"terraform-s100","q":"In Terraform, how do you set the instance type of an Elastic Beanstalk environment?","a":"<p>Add a <code>setting</code> with <code>namespace = \"aws:autoscaling:launchconfiguration\"</code>, <code>name = \"InstanceType\"</code> and <code>value = \"t2.micro\"</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>resource &quot;aws_elastic_beanstalk_environment&quot; &quot;env&quot; { name = &quot;my-eb-env&quot;, application = aws_elastic_beanstalk_application.app.name, solution_stack_name = &quot;64bit Amazon Linux 2 v3.3.13 running Python 3.8&quot;, setting = { namespace = &quot;aws:autoscaling:launchconfiguration&quot;, name = &quot;InstanceType&quot;, value = &quot;t2.micro&quot; } }</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0278","card":"q-terraform-101-elastic-beanstalk-application","sec":"terraform-s100","q":"In Terraform, how do you deploy an application version to Elastic Beanstalk from S3?","a":"<p>Create a bucket, upload <code>app.zip</code> as an <code>aws_s3_object</code>, then create <code>aws_elastic_beanstalk_application_version</code> with the bucket and key.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>resource &quot;aws_s3_bucket&quot; &quot;app_bucket&quot; { bucket = &quot;my-eb-app-bucket&quot; }\nresource &quot;aws_s3_object&quot; &quot;app_version&quot; { bucket = aws_s3_bucket.app_bucket.bucket, key = &quot;app.zip&quot;, source = &quot;path/to/your/app.zip&quot; }\nresource &quot;aws_elastic_beanstalk_application_version&quot; &quot;version&quot; { name = &quot;v1&quot;, application = aws_elastic_beanstalk_application.app.name, bucket = aws_s3_bucket.app_bucket.bucket, key = aws_s3_object.app_version.key }</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0279","card":"q-terraform-102-debug-terraform-ec2-instance-not-accessi","sec":"terraform-s101","q":"In Terraform, which <code>aws_instance</code> settings make an EC2 instance reachable from outside?","a":"<p>Put it in a public subnet, attach the SSH security group and set <code>associate_public_ip_address = true</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>resource &quot;aws_instance&quot; &quot;example&quot; { ami = &quot;ami-0c55b159cbfafe1f0&quot;, instance_type = &quot;t2.micro&quot;, subnet_id = aws_subnet.public.id, security_groups = [aws_security_group.allow_ssh.id], associate_public_ip_address = true }</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0280","card":"q-terraform-102-debug-terraform-ec2-instance-not-accessi","sec":"terraform-s101","q":"Which commands apply the fix for an inaccessible EC2 instance and inspect it?","a":"<p><code>terraform apply</code>, then <code>aws ec2 describe-instances</code> with <code>--instance-ids</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>terraform apply\naws ec2 describe-instances --instance-ids &lt;instance-id&gt;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0281","card":"q-terraform-103-add-iam-policy-to-existing-role","sec":"terraform-s102","q":"In Terraform, how do you add a new policy to an existing IAM role?","a":"<p>Define an <code>aws_iam_policy</code>, then attach it with <code>aws_iam_role_policy_attachment</code> using the role name and the policy ARN.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>resource &quot;aws_iam_policy&quot; &quot;new_policy&quot; { name = &quot;new-policy&quot;, policy = jsonencode({ Version = &quot;2012-10-17&quot;, Statement = [{ Action = &quot;s3:GetObject&quot;, Effect = &quot;Allow&quot;, Resource = &quot;arn:aws:s3:::my-bucket/*&quot; }] }) }\nresource &quot;aws_iam_role_policy_attachment&quot; &quot;attach&quot; { role = aws_iam_role.existing_role.name, policy_arn = aws_iam_policy.new_policy.arn }</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0282","card":"q-terraform-103-add-iam-policy-to-existing-role","sec":"terraform-s102","q":"In Terraform, what permission does an <code>aws_iam_policy</code> named <code>new-policy</code> grant, and on which resource?","a":"<p><code>s3:GetObject</code> with <code>Effect = \"Allow\"</code> on <code>arn:aws:s3:::my-bucket/*</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>resource &quot;aws_iam_policy&quot; &quot;new_policy&quot; { name = &quot;new-policy&quot;, policy = jsonencode({ Version = &quot;2012-10-17&quot;, Statement = [{ Action = &quot;s3:GetObject&quot;, Effect = &quot;Allow&quot;, Resource = &quot;arn:aws:s3:::my-bucket/*&quot; }] }) }</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0283","card":"q-terraform-104-scale-eks-node-group-to-3-nodes","sec":"terraform-s103","q":"In Terraform, how do you scale an EKS node group to 3 nodes?","a":"<p>Set <code>desired_size = 3</code> in <code>scaling_config</code>, with <code>max_size = 5</code> and <code>min_size = 1</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>resource &quot;aws_eks_node_group&quot; &quot;example&quot; { cluster_name = aws_eks_cluster.example.name, node_group_name = &quot;my-node-group&quot;, node_role_arn = aws_iam_role.node.arn, subnet_ids = aws_subnet.example[*].id, scaling_config = { desired_size = 3, max_size = 5, min_size = 1 } }</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0284","card":"q-terraform-105-debug-terraform-lambda-function-failure","sec":"terraform-s104","q":"In Terraform, which arguments define the <code>aws_lambda_function</code> that is being debugged?","a":"<p><code>function_name = \"my-lambda\"</code>, <code>handler = \"index.handler\"</code>, <code>runtime = \"nodejs16.x\"</code>, <code>role</code> with the role ARN and <code>filename = \"lambda.zip\"</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>resource &quot;aws_lambda_function&quot; &quot;example&quot; { function_name = &quot;my-lambda&quot;, handler = &quot;index.handler&quot;, runtime = &quot;nodejs16.x&quot;, role = aws_iam_role.lambda.arn, filename = &quot;lambda.zip&quot; }</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0285","card":"q-terraform-106-fix-terraform-ec2-launch-issue-verify-wi","sec":"terraform-s105","q":"In Terraform, which settings does the EC2 launch fix use?","a":"<p><code>subnet_id</code> of a public subnet, the SSH security group, and <code>associate_public_ip_address = true</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>resource &quot;aws_instance&quot; &quot;example&quot; { ami = &quot;ami-0c55b159cbfafe1f0&quot;, instance_type = &quot;t2.micro&quot;, subnet_id = aws_subnet.public.id, security_groups = [aws_security_group.allow_ssh.id], associate_public_ip_address = true }</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0286","card":"q-terraform-106-fix-terraform-ec2-launch-issue-verify-wi","sec":"terraform-s105","q":"Which commands verify an EC2 launch fix and show the instance ID and state?","a":"<p><code>terraform apply</code>, then <code>aws ec2 describe-instances</code> with a <code>--query</code> for <code>InstanceId</code> and <code>State.Name</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>terraform apply\naws ec2 describe-instances --instance-ids &lt;instance-id&gt; --query &quot;Reservations[*].Instances[*].[InstanceId, State.Name]&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0287","card":"q-terraform-107-debug-terraform-auto-scaling-group-not-s","sec":"terraform-s106","q":"In Terraform, which sizes and subnets does the Auto Scaling group <code>my-asg</code> set?","a":"<p><code>min_size = 1</code>, <code>max_size = 3</code>, <code>desired_capacity = 2</code>, and <code>vpc_zone_identifier</code> with two subnets. It uses a launch template at <code>$Latest</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>resource &quot;aws_autoscaling_group&quot; &quot;example&quot; { name = &quot;my-asg&quot;, min_size = 1, max_size = 3, desired_capacity = 2, vpc_zone_identifier = [aws_subnet.subnet1.id, aws_subnet.subnet2.id], launch_template = { id = aws_launch_template.example.id, version = &quot;$Latest&quot; } }</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0288","card":"q-terraform-107-debug-terraform-auto-scaling-group-not-s","sec":"terraform-s106","q":"Which AWS CLI commands help debug an Auto Scaling group that is not scaling?","a":"<p><code>describe-auto-scaling-groups</code>, <code>describe-scaling-activities</code> with <code>--max-items 10</code>, and <code>aws ec2 describe-instances</code> for the group instances.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>aws autoscaling describe-auto-scaling-groups --auto-scaling-group-names my-asg\naws autoscaling describe-scaling-activities --auto-scaling-group-name my-asg --max-items 10\naws ec2 describe-instances --instance-ids &lt;instance-ids-from-asg&gt;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0289","card":"q-terraform-108-create-sns-topic-with-terraform-subscrib","sec":"terraform-s107","q":"In Terraform, how do you expose an SNS topic ARN as an output?","a":"<p>Create the <code>aws_sns_topic</code> and add an <code>output \"sns_topic_arn\"</code> with <code>value = aws_sns_topic.example.arn</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Hcl</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>resource &quot;aws_sns_topic&quot; &quot;example&quot; { name = &quot;my-sns-topic&quot; }\noutput &quot;sns_topic_arn&quot; { value = aws_sns_topic.example.arn }</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0290","card":"q-terraform-108-create-sns-topic-with-terraform-subscrib","sec":"terraform-s107","q":"Which command subscribes an email address to an SNS topic with the AWS CLI?","a":"<p><code>aws sns subscribe</code> with <code>--topic-arn</code>, <code>--protocol email</code> and <code>--notification-endpoint</code>. Run <code>terraform apply</code> first.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>terraform apply\naws sns subscribe --topic-arn &lt;sns-topic-arn&gt; --protocol email --notification-endpoint user@example.com</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0291","card":"q-terraform-109-check-ec2-status-reboot-if-unresponsive","sec":"terraform-s108","q":"Which AWS CLI command prints the state name of an EC2 instance?","a":"<p><code>aws ec2 describe-instances</code> with <code>--query</code> for <code>State.Name</code> and <code>--output text</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>aws ec2 describe-instances --instance-ids &lt;instance-id&gt; --query &quot;Reservations[*].Instances[*].State.Name&quot; --output text</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0292","card":"q-terraform-109-check-ec2-status-reboot-if-unresponsive","sec":"terraform-s108","q":"Which AWS CLI command reboots an unresponsive EC2 instance?","a":"<p><code>aws ec2 reboot-instances --instance-ids &lt;instance-id&gt;</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>aws ec2 reboot-instances --instance-ids &lt;instance-id&gt;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0293","card":"q-terraform-110-identify-terminate-ec2-instances-older-t","sec":"terraform-s109","q":"Which one-line AWS CLI command finds EC2 instances launched more than 30 days ago and terminates them?","a":"<p>It queries <code>LaunchTime</code> against a date 30 days ago, then pipes the instance IDs through <code>xargs -r</code> into <code>aws ec2 terminate-instances</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>aws ec2 describe-instances --query &quot;Reservations[*].Instances[?LaunchTime&lt;&#x27;$(date -u -d &#x27;30 days ago&#x27; +%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ&#x27;)&#x27;].InstanceId&quot; --output text | xargs -r aws ec2 terminate-instances --instance-ids</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0294","card":"q-terraform-111-move-old-s3-files-to-glacier","sec":"terraform-s110","q":"Which AWS CLI command moves S3 objects older than 30 days to Glacier?","a":"<p>List objects with <code>list-objects-v2</code>, filter by <code>LastModified</code>, and pass each key to <code>aws s3api put-object</code> with <code>--storage-class GLACIER</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>aws s3api list-objects-v2 --bucket &lt;bucket-name&gt; --query &quot;Contents[?LastModified&lt;&#x27;$(date -u -d &#x27;30 days ago&#x27; +%Y-%m-%d&#x27;)&#x27;].Key&quot; --output text | xargs -I {} aws s3api put-object --bucket &lt;bucket-name&gt; --key {} --storage-class GLACIER</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0295","card":"q-terraform-112-troubleshoot-auto-scaling-group-not-laun","sec":"terraform-s111","q":"Which AWS CLI commands troubleshoot an Auto Scaling group that is not launching instances?","a":"<p><code>aws autoscaling describe-auto-scaling-groups</code> to see the group, and <code>describe-scaling-activities</code> with <code>--max-items 10</code> to see recent activities.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>aws autoscaling describe-auto-scaling-groups --auto-scaling-group-names &lt;asg-name&gt;\naws autoscaling describe-scaling-activities --auto-scaling-group-name &lt;asg-name&gt; --max-items 10</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0296","card":"q-terraform-113-fetch-last-10-minutes-of-ecs-task-logs","sec":"terraform-s112","q":"Which AWS CLI command fetches the last 10 minutes of ECS task logs?","a":"<p><code>aws logs get-log-events</code> with the log group and stream names, <code>--start-time</code> set to 10 minutes ago and <code>--end-time</code> set to now, both in milliseconds.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>aws logs get-log-events --log-group-name &lt;log-group-name&gt; --log-stream-name &lt;log-stream-name&gt; --start-time $(date -d &#x27;10 minutes ago&#x27; +%s000) --end-time $(date +%s000) --output text</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0297","card":"q-terraform-114-check-rds-status-initiate-failover","sec":"terraform-s113","q":"Which AWS CLI command prints the status of an RDS instance?","a":"<p><code>aws rds describe-db-instances</code> with <code>--query</code> for <code>DBInstanceStatus</code> and <code>--output text</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>aws rds describe-db-instances --db-instance-identifier &lt;db-instance-id&gt; --query &quot;DBInstances[*].DBInstanceStatus&quot; --output text</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0298","card":"q-terraform-114-check-rds-status-initiate-failover","sec":"terraform-s113","q":"Which AWS CLI command starts an RDS failover?","a":"<p><code>aws rds failover-db-cluster --db-cluster-identifier &lt;db-cluster-id&gt;</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>aws rds failover-db-cluster --db-cluster-identifier &lt;db-cluster-id&gt;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0299","card":"q-terraform-115-delete-unused-elastic-ips","sec":"terraform-s114","q":"Which AWS CLI command releases unused Elastic IPs?","a":"<p>It selects addresses where <code>AssociationId==null</code> with <code>describe-addresses</code>, then pipes the allocation IDs through <code>xargs -r</code> into <code>aws ec2 release-address --allocation-id</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>aws ec2 describe-addresses --query &quot;Addresses[?AssociationId==null].AllocationId&quot; --output text | xargs -r aws ec2 release-address --allocation-id</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0300","card":"q-terraform-116-check-lambda-function-failure-logs","sec":"terraform-s115","q":"Which AWS CLI command shows recent error logs of a Lambda function?","a":"<p><code>aws logs filter-log-events</code> on the log group <code>/aws/lambda/&lt;function-name&gt;</code>, with <code>--filter-pattern \"ERROR\"</code> and <code>--limit 10</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>aws logs filter-log-events --log-group-name /aws/lambda/&lt;function-name&gt; --filter-pattern &quot;ERROR&quot; --limit 10</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0301","card":"q-terraform-117-investigate-elb-unhealthy-instances-dere","sec":"terraform-s116","q":"Which AWS CLI command lists unhealthy targets of a target group?","a":"<p><code>aws elbv2 describe-target-health</code> with a <code>--query</code> that keeps targets whose state is <code>unhealthy</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>aws elbv2 describe-target-health --target-group-arn &lt;target-group-arn&gt; --query &quot;TargetHealthDescriptions[?TargetHealth.State==&#x27;unhealthy&#x27;].Target.Id&quot; --output text</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0302","card":"q-terraform-117-investigate-elb-unhealthy-instances-dere","sec":"terraform-s116","q":"Which AWS CLI command removes an instance from a target group?","a":"<p><code>aws elbv2 deregister-targets</code> with <code>--target-group-arn</code> and <code>--targets Id=&lt;instance-id&gt;</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>aws elbv2 deregister-targets --target-group-arn &lt;target-group-arn&gt; --targets Id=&lt;instance-id&gt;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0303","card":"q-terraform-118-update-ec2-security-group-for-https","sec":"terraform-s117","q":"Which AWS CLI command opens port 443 on an EC2 security group?","a":"<p><code>aws ec2 authorize-security-group-ingress</code> with <code>--protocol tcp</code>, <code>--port 443</code> and <code>--cidr 0.0.0.0/0</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>aws ec2 authorize-security-group-ingress --group-id &lt;security-group-id&gt; --protocol tcp --port 443 --cidr 0.0.0.0/0</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0304","card":"q-terraform-119-check-s3-bucket-replication-rule-status","sec":"terraform-s118","q":"Which AWS CLI command shows the replication rules of an S3 bucket?","a":"<p><code>aws s3api get-bucket-replication --bucket &lt;source-bucket-name&gt;</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>aws s3api get-bucket-replication --bucket &lt;source-bucket-name&gt;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0305","card":"q-terraform-120-troubleshoot-eks-cluster-not-responding","sec":"terraform-s119","q":"Which three AWS CLI commands troubleshoot an unresponsive EKS cluster?","a":"<p><code>describe-cluster</code> with a query for <code>cluster.status</code>, <code>list-nodegroups</code>, and <code>describe-nodegroup</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>aws eks describe-cluster --name &lt;cluster-name&gt; --query &quot;cluster.status&quot;\naws eks list-nodegroups --cluster-name &lt;cluster-name&gt;\naws eks describe-nodegroup --cluster-name &lt;cluster-name&gt; --nodegroup-name &lt;nodegroup-name&gt;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0306","card":"q-terraform-120-troubleshoot-eks-cluster-not-responding","sec":"terraform-s119","q":"Which AWS CLI command shows the status of an EKS cluster?","a":"<p><code>aws eks describe-cluster</code> with <code>--name</code> and <code>--query \"cluster.status\"</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>aws eks describe-cluster --name &lt;cluster-name&gt; --query &quot;cluster.status&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0307","card":"q-terraform-121-restore-s3-object-from-specific-version","sec":"terraform-s120","q":"Which AWS CLI command restores an S3 object from a specific version?","a":"<p>Copy the object onto itself with <code>aws s3api copy-object</code>, using <code>--copy-source</code> with <code>?versionId=&lt;version-id&gt;</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>aws s3api copy-object --bucket &lt;bucket-name&gt; --key &lt;object-key&gt; --copy-source &lt;bucket-name&gt;/&lt;object-key&gt;?versionId=&lt;version-id&gt;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0308","card":"q-terraform-122-troubleshoot-cloudwatch-alarm-not-trigge","sec":"terraform-s121","q":"Which AWS CLI commands troubleshoot a CloudWatch alarm that does not trigger?","a":"<p><code>aws cloudwatch describe-alarms</code> with <code>--alarm-names</code>, and <code>describe-alarm-history</code> with <code>--history-item-type StateUpdate</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>aws cloudwatch describe-alarms --alarm-names &lt;alarm-name&gt;\naws cloudwatch describe-alarm-history --alarm-name &lt;alarm-name&gt; --history-item-type StateUpdate</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0309","card":"q-terraform-123-resize-rds-instance-for-load","sec":"terraform-s122","q":"Which AWS CLI command changes the instance class of an RDS instance right away?","a":"<p><code>aws rds modify-db-instance</code> with <code>--db-instance-class &lt;new-instance-class&gt;</code> and <code>--apply-immediately</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>aws rds modify-db-instance --db-instance-identifier &lt;db-instance-id&gt; --db-instance-class &lt;new-instance-class&gt; --apply-immediately</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0310","card":"q-terraform-124-how-python-integrates-with-terraform","sec":"terraform-s123","q":"How does Python integrate with Terraform for resource management?","a":"<p>The <code>python-terraform</code> library or the <code>subprocess</code> module can execute Terraform commands or manage state files. Python's versatility and rich ecosystem make it a good orchestrator for Terraform alongside other tools.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"terraform-f0311","card":"q-terraform-124-how-python-integrates-with-terraform","sec":"terraform-s123","q":"How is idempotency ensured with Terraform?","a":"<p>Terraform uses state files so resources are only created or updated when needed.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"terraform-f0312","card":"q-terraform-125-purpose-of-python-terraform","sec":"terraform-s124","q":"What is the purpose of the Terraform Python provider (<code>python-terraform</code>), and how can it be used to manage infrastructure?","a":"<p>It is a library that lets Python scripts interact with Terraform commands and state files. It is used to:</p>\n<ul>\n  <li>Execute Terraform commands (<code>init</code>, <code>plan</code>, <code>apply</code>) programmatically.</li>\n  <li>Read or modify Terraform state files.</li>\n  <li>Automate infrastructure provisioning in workflows.</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>from python_terraform import Terraform\ntf = Terraform(working_dir=&#x27;.&#x27;)\ntf.init()\ntf.apply(skip_plan=True)</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"terraform-f0313","card":"q-terraform-126-state-management-from-python","sec":"terraform-s125","q":"How do you handle state management in Terraform when using Python to automate workflows?","a":"<p>Terraform state is kept in a <code>terraform.tfstate</code> file. With Python:</p>\n<ul>\n  <li>Use <code>python-terraform</code> to read and write state files.</li>\n  <li>Store state in remote backends (for example S3) for team collaboration.</li>\n  <li>Lock state using DynamoDB to prevent concurrent modifications.</li>\n  <li>Avoid manual state edits to prevent drift.</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>from python_terraform import Terraform\ntf = Terraform(working_dir=&#x27;.&#x27;)\nstate = tf.read_state_file()\nprint(state)</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"terraform-f0314","card":"q-terraform-127-how-do-you-use-the-python-terraform-libr","sec":"terraform-s126","q":"In Python, how do you install the <code>python-terraform</code> library?","a":"<p>Run <code>pip install python-terraform</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0315","card":"q-terraform-127-how-do-you-use-the-python-terraform-libr","sec":"terraform-s126","q":"In Python, how do you run <code>terraform init</code> with <code>python-terraform</code> and check the result?","a":"<p>Create <code>Terraform(working_dir=...)</code>, call <code>tf.init()</code>, which returns <code>return_code, stdout, stderr</code>. A <code>return_code</code> of 0 means success.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>from python_terraform import Terraform\n\n# Initialize Terraform\ntf = Terraform(working_dir=&#x27;/path/to/terraform/project&#x27;)\n\n# Run Terraform init\nreturn_code, stdout, stderr = tf.init()\nif return_code == 0:\n    print(&quot;Terraform init successful&quot;)\nelse:\n    print(f&quot;Terraform init failed: {stderr}&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0316","card":"q-terraform-128-write-a-python-script-to-initialize-and","sec":"terraform-s127","q":"In Python, how do you initialize and apply a Terraform configuration with <code>python-terraform</code>?","a":"<p>Call <code>tf.init()</code>, exit if it fails, then call <code>tf.apply(auto_approve=True)</code> and check the return code.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>from python_terraform import Terraform\n\n# Initialize Terraform\ntf = Terraform(working_dir=&#x27;/path/to/terraform/project&#x27;)\n\n# Run Terraform init\nreturn_code, stdout, stderr = tf.init()\nif return_code != 0:\n    print(f&quot;Init failed: {stderr}&quot;)\n    exit(1)\n\n# Run Terraform apply\nreturn_code, stdout, stderr = tf.apply(auto_approve=True)\nif return_code == 0:\n    print(&quot;Apply successful&quot;)\nelse:\n    print(f&quot;Apply failed: {stderr}&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0317","card":"q-terraform-128-write-a-python-script-to-initialize-and","sec":"terraform-s127","q":"In <code>python-terraform</code>, which argument makes <code>apply</code> skip the interactive approval?","a":"<p><code>auto_approve=True</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>return_code, stdout, stderr = tf.apply(auto_approve=True)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0318","card":"q-terraform-129-how-do-you-manage-terraform-state-files","sec":"terraform-s128","q":"In Python, how do you read Terraform state with <code>python-terraform</code>?","a":"<p>Call <code>tf.state_pull()</code> and parse the result with <code>json.loads</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>state = tf.state_pull()\nstate_data = json.loads(state)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0319","card":"q-terraform-129-how-do-you-manage-terraform-state-files","sec":"terraform-s128","q":"In Python, how do you list the resources in the Terraform state data?","a":"<p>Loop over <code>state_data['resources']</code> and print each resource <code>type</code> and <code>name</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import json\nfrom python_terraform import Terraform\n\n# Initialize Terraform\ntf = Terraform(working_dir=&#x27;/path/to/terraform/project&#x27;)\n\n# Read state\nstate = tf.state_pull()\nstate_data = json.loads(state)\n\n# Example: List resources\nfor resource in state_data[&#x27;resources&#x27;]:\n    print(f&quot;Resource: {resource[&#x27;type&#x27;]}.{resource[&#x27;name&#x27;]}&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0320","card":"q-terraform-130-explain-how-to-use-python-to-parse-terra","sec":"terraform-s129","q":"In Python, how do you save a Terraform plan and read its resource changes with <code>python-terraform</code>?","a":"<p>Run <code>tf.plan</code> with <code>out=\"plan.tfplan\"</code>, then <code>tf.show(\"plan.tfplan\", format=\"json\")</code> and read <code>resource_changes</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>from python_terraform import Terraform, IsFlagged\n\n# Initialize Terraform\ntf = Terraform(working_dir=&#x27;/path/to/terraform/project&#x27;)\n\n# Run Terraform plan with JSON output\nreturn_code, stdout, stderr = tf.plan(out=&quot;plan.tfplan&quot;, var={&#x27;instance_type&#x27;: &#x27;t2.micro&#x27;}, input=IsFlagged.NO)\n\n# Parse plan output\nplan_data = tf.show(&quot;plan.tfplan&quot;, format=&quot;json&quot;)\nchanges = plan_data[&#x27;resource_changes&#x27;]\nfor change in changes:\n    print(f&quot;Resource: {change[&#x27;address&#x27;]}, Action: {change[&#x27;change&#x27;][&#x27;actions&#x27;]}&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0321","card":"q-terraform-130-explain-how-to-use-python-to-parse-terra","sec":"terraform-s129","q":"In <code>python-terraform</code>, which argument stops <code>plan</code> from prompting for input?","a":"<p><code>input=IsFlagged.NO</code>, with <code>IsFlagged</code> imported from <code>python_terraform</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>return_code, stdout, stderr = tf.plan(out=&quot;plan.tfplan&quot;, var={&#x27;instance_type&#x27;: &#x27;t2.micro&#x27;}, input=IsFlagged.NO)\nfrom python_terraform import Terraform, IsFlagged</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0322","card":"q-terraform-131-write-a-python-script-to-create-a-terraf","sec":"terraform-s130","q":"In Python, how do you write a Terraform variable file in JSON format?","a":"<p>Build a dict of variables and use <code>json.dump</code> to write <code>terraform.tfvars.json</code> with <code>indent=2</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import json\n\n# Define variables\nvariables = {\n    &#x27;instance_type&#x27;: &#x27;t2.micro&#x27;,\n    &#x27;region&#x27;: &#x27;us-east-1&#x27;,\n    &#x27;ami_id&#x27;: &#x27;ami-12345678&#x27;\n}\n\n# Write to JSON .tfvars file\nwith open(&#x27;terraform.tfvars.json&#x27;, &#x27;w&#x27;) as f:\n    json.dump(variables, f, indent=2)\n\n# Alternatively, write to HCL .tfvars file\nwith open(&#x27;terraform.tfvars&#x27;, &#x27;w&#x27;) as f:\n    for key, value in variables.items():\n        f.write(f&#x27;{key} = &quot;{value}&quot;\\n&#x27;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0323","card":"q-terraform-131-write-a-python-script-to-create-a-terraf","sec":"terraform-s130","q":"In Python, how do you write variables to an HCL <code>.tfvars</code> file?","a":"<p>Open <code>terraform.tfvars</code> for writing and write each pair as <code>key = \"value\"</code> with a newline.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>with open(&#x27;terraform.tfvars&#x27;, &#x27;w&#x27;) as f:\n    for key, value in variables.items():\n        f.write(f&#x27;{key} = &quot;{value}&quot;\\n&#x27;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0324","card":"q-terraform-132-how-do-you-handle-terraform-errors-in-py","sec":"terraform-s131","q":"In Python, how do you detect a failed Terraform command with <code>python-terraform</code>?","a":"<p>Check that <code>return_code</code> is not 0 and print or parse <code>stderr</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>from python_terraform import Terraform\n\n# Initialize Terraform\ntf = Terraform(working_dir=&#x27;/path/to/terraform/project&#x27;)\n\ntry:\n    return_code, stdout, stderr = tf.apply(auto_approve=True)\n    if return_code != 0:\n        print(f&quot;Terraform error: {stderr}&quot;)\n    else:\n        print(&quot;Terraform applied successfully&quot;)\nexcept Exception as e:\n    print(f&quot;Unexpected error: {e}&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0325","card":"q-terraform-132-how-do-you-handle-terraform-errors-in-py","sec":"terraform-s131","q":"In Python, how do you guard Terraform calls against unexpected exceptions?","a":"<p>Wrap the call in <code>try</code>/<code>except Exception</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>try:\nexcept Exception as e:</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0326","card":"q-terraform-133-how-can-python-be-used-to-automate-terra","sec":"terraform-s132","q":"In <code>python-terraform</code>, which methods create, select and delete a Terraform workspace?","a":"<p><code>workspace_new</code>, <code>workspace_select</code> and <code>workspace_delete</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>from python_terraform import Terraform\n\n# Initialize Terraform\ntf = Terraform(working_dir=&#x27;/path/to/terraform/project&#x27;)\n\n# Create a new workspace\ntf.workspace_new(&quot;dev&quot;)\n\n# Select a workspace\ntf.workspace_select(&quot;dev&quot;)\n\n# List workspaces\nreturn_code, stdout, stderr = tf.workspace_list()\nprint(f&quot;Workspaces: {stdout.split()}&quot;)\n\n# Delete a workspace\ntf.workspace_delete(&quot;dev&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0327","card":"q-terraform-133-how-can-python-be-used-to-automate-terra","sec":"terraform-s132","q":"In <code>python-terraform</code>, which method lists workspaces?","a":"<p><code>tf.workspace_list()</code>, which returns <code>return_code, stdout, stderr</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>return_code, stdout, stderr = tf.workspace_list()\nprint(f&quot;Workspaces: {stdout.split()}&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0328","card":"q-terraform-134-write-a-python-script-to-destroy-terrafo","sec":"terraform-s133","q":"In Python, how do you destroy Terraform-managed resources with <code>python-terraform</code>?","a":"<p>Call <code>tf.destroy(auto_approve=True)</code> and check the return code.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>from python_terraform import Terraform\n\n# Initialize Terraform\ntf = Terraform(working_dir=&#x27;/path/to/terraform/project&#x27;)\n\n# Run Terraform destroy\nreturn_code, stdout, stderr = tf.destroy(auto_approve=True)\nif return_code == 0:\n    print(&quot;Resources destroyed successfully&quot;)\nelse:\n    print(f&quot;Destroy failed: {stderr}&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0329","card":"q-terraform-135-how-do-you-integrate-python-with-terrafo","sec":"terraform-s134","q":"In Python, how do you combine <code>python-terraform</code> and <code>boto3</code> to manage AWS resources?","a":"<p>Use <code>python-terraform</code> to apply the configuration, then <code>boto3</code> to validate or modify the AWS resources after deployment.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0330","card":"q-terraform-135-how-do-you-integrate-python-with-terrafo","sec":"terraform-s134","q":"In Python, how do you pass a variable to <code>apply</code> and check EC2 instances with <code>boto3</code> afterwards?","a":"<p>Pass <code>var={'instance_type': 't2.micro'}</code> to <code>tf.apply</code>, then call <code>describe_instances</code> on a <code>boto3</code> EC2 client.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import boto3\nfrom python_terraform import Terraform\n\n# Initialize Terraform\ntf = Terraform(working_dir=&#x27;/path/to/terraform/project&#x27;)\n\n# Apply Terraform configuration\ntf.apply(auto_approve=True, var={&#x27;instance_type&#x27;: &#x27;t2.micro&#x27;})\n\n# Validate with boto3\nec2 = boto3.client(&#x27;ec2&#x27;)\nresponse = ec2.describe_instances()\nfor reservation in response[&#x27;Reservations&#x27;]:\n    for instance in reservation[&#x27;Instances&#x27;]:\n        print(f&quot;Instance ID: {instance[&#x27;InstanceId&#x27;]}, Type: {instance[&#x27;InstanceType&#x27;]}&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0331","card":"q-terraform-136-explain-how-to-use-python-to-validate-te","sec":"terraform-s135","q":"In Python, how do you validate a Terraform configuration before applying it?","a":"<p>Call <code>tf.validate()</code> and check that <code>return_code</code> is 0.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>from python_terraform import Terraform\n\n# Initialize Terraform\ntf = Terraform(working_dir=&#x27;/path/to/terraform/project&#x27;)\n\n# Validate configuration\nreturn_code, stdout, stderr = tf.validate()\nif return_code == 0:\n    print(&quot;Configuration is valid&quot;)\nelse:\n    print(f&quot;Validation failed: {stderr}&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0332","card":"q-terraform-137-your-team-needs-to-automate-the-deployme","sec":"terraform-s136","q":"In Python, how do you structure a script that deploys an AWS EKS cluster with Terraform?","a":"<p>Use <code>python-terraform</code> (or <code>subprocess</code>) to run <code>init</code>, then <code>plan</code>, then <code>apply</code>. Raise an exception when any step returns a non-zero code.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>from python_terraform import Terraform\nimport os\n\ndef deploy_eks_cluster(working_dir):\n    tf = Terraform(working_dir=working_dir)\n    os.environ[&quot;AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID&quot;] = os.getenv(&quot;AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID&quot;)\n    os.environ[&quot;AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY&quot;] = os.getenv(&quot;AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY&quot;)\n\n    # Initialize Terraform\n    return_code, stdout, stderr = tf.init()\n    if return_code != 0:\n        raise Exception(f&quot;Terraform init failed: {stderr}&quot;)\n\n    # Generate and show plan\n    return_code, stdout, stderr = tf.plan()\n    if return_code != 0:\n        raise Exception(f&quot;Terraform plan failed: {stderr}&quot;)\n    print(&quot;Terraform Plan:&quot;, stdout)\n\n    # Apply configuration\n    return_code, stdout, stderr = tf.apply(skip_plan=True)\n    if return_code != 0:\n        raise Exception(f&quot;Terraform apply failed: {stderr}&quot;)\n    print(&quot;EKS cluster deployed!&quot;)\n\n# Example usage\ndeploy_eks_cluster(&quot;./terraform/eks&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0333","card":"q-terraform-137-your-team-needs-to-automate-the-deployme","sec":"terraform-s136","q":"In Python, how does a script that deploys an EKS cluster with Terraform pass AWS credentials to Terraform?","a":"<p>It copies <code>AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID</code> and <code>AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY</code> with <code>os.getenv</code> into <code>os.environ</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import os\n    os.environ[&quot;AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID&quot;] = os.getenv(&quot;AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID&quot;)\n    os.environ[&quot;AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY&quot;] = os.getenv(&quot;AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0334","card":"q-terraform-138-a-terraform-configuration-is-causing-res","sec":"terraform-s137","q":"In Python, how do you detect drift between AWS and Terraform state?","a":"<p>Use <code>boto3</code> to compare current AWS resources with the state file. If they differ, update the configuration or reapply it.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0335","card":"q-terraform-138-a-terraform-configuration-is-causing-res","sec":"terraform-s137","q":"In Python, in a script that detects Terraform drift with <code>boto3</code>, how are drifted EC2 instances computed?","a":"<p>It builds a set of instance IDs from the state and a set from <code>describe_instances</code>, then subtracts the state set from the AWS set.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>    tf_instances = {r[&quot;attributes&quot;][&quot;instance_id&quot;] for r in tf_state[&quot;resources&quot;] if r[&quot;type&quot;] == &quot;aws_instance&quot;}\n    aws_instances = {i[&quot;InstanceId&quot;] for r in response[&quot;Reservations&quot;] for i in r[&quot;Instances&quot;]}\n    drifted_instances = aws_instances - tf_instances</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0336","card":"q-terraform-138-a-terraform-configuration-is-causing-res","sec":"terraform-s137","q":"In Python, in a script that detects Terraform drift with <code>boto3</code>, how are drifted instances reconciled?","a":"<p>It runs <code>terraform import</code> for each one with <code>subprocess.run</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>            subprocess.run([&quot;terraform&quot;, &quot;import&quot;, f&quot;aws_instance.instance_{instance_id}&quot;, instance_id], check=True)\n        # Reconcile by importing or destroying drifted resources</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0337","card":"q-terraform-139-your-terraform-configuration-is-failing","sec":"terraform-s138","q":"In Python, how do you validate an AWS region before applying Terraform?","a":"<p>Use <code>boto3</code> to call <code>describe_regions</code> with the region, and <code>python-terraform</code> to run <code>validate</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import boto3\nimport botocore\nfrom python_terraform import Terraform\n\ndef validate_terraform_config(working_dir, region):\n    ec2 = boto3.client(&quot;ec2&quot;, region_name=region)\n    try:\n        ec2.describe_regions(RegionNames=[region])\n        print(f&quot;Region {region} is valid&quot;)\n    except botocore.exceptions.ClientError:\n        raise Exception(f&quot;Invalid AWS region: {region}&quot;)\n\n    tf = Terraform(working_dir=working_dir)\n    return_code, stdout, stderr = tf.validate()\n    if return_code != 0:\n        raise Exception(f&quot;Terraform validation failed: {stderr}&quot;)\n    print(&quot;Terraform configuration is valid&quot;)\n\n# Example usage\nvalidate_terraform_config(&quot;./terraform&quot;, &quot;us-east-1&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0338","card":"q-terraform-139-your-terraform-configuration-is-failing","sec":"terraform-s138","q":"In Python, which exception signals an invalid region when a script validates an AWS region with <code>describe_regions</code>?","a":"<p><code>botocore.exceptions.ClientError</code> from <code>describe_regions</code>, which the script turns into an \"Invalid AWS region\" exception.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>    except botocore.exceptions.ClientError:\n        raise Exception(f&quot;Invalid AWS region: {region}&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0339","card":"q-terraform-140-your-python-script-managing-terraform-re","sec":"terraform-s139","q":"How do you make a Python script that manages Terraform resources idempotent?","a":"<p>Check existing resources with <code>boto3</code> before creating them, check the Terraform state file to avoid duplicates, and lock state with S3 or DynamoDB.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0340","card":"q-terraform-140-your-python-script-managing-terraform-re","sec":"terraform-s139","q":"In Python, how does an idempotent script check whether an EC2 instance already exists before creating it?","a":"<p>It calls <code>describe_instances</code> with a <code>tag:Name</code> filter and returns early if <code>Reservations</code> is not empty.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import boto3\nfrom python_terraform import Terraform\n\ndef create_instance_if_not_exists(instance_name, working_dir):\n    ec2 = boto3.client(&quot;ec2&quot;)\n    response = ec2.describe_instances(Filters=[{&quot;Name&quot;: &quot;tag:Name&quot;, &quot;Values&quot;: [instance_name]}])\n    if response[&quot;Reservations&quot;]:\n        print(f&quot;Instance {instance_name} already exists&quot;)\n        return\n\n    tf = Terraform(working_dir=working_dir)\n    tf.apply(var={&quot;instance_name&quot;: instance_name}, skip_plan=True)\n    print(f&quot;Instance {instance_name} created&quot;)\n\n# Example usage\ncreate_instance_if_not_exists(&quot;my-instance&quot;, &quot;./terraform&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0341","card":"q-terraform-141-your-team-needs-to-automate-the-cleanup","sec":"terraform-s140","q":"In Python, how do you find and delete unused AWS resources with Terraform?","a":"<p>Use <code>boto3</code> to list resources and compare them with the Terraform state. Delete unused ones with <code>boto3</code> or update the configuration.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0342","card":"q-terraform-141-your-team-needs-to-automate-the-cleanup","sec":"terraform-s140","q":"In Python, in a script that cleans up unused EC2 instances, how are they terminated?","a":"<p>It subtracts instance IDs in state from those in AWS, then calls <code>terminate_instances</code> for each remaining ID.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>    unused_instances = aws_instances - tf_instances\n        ec2.terminate_instances(InstanceIds=[instance_id])</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0343","card":"q-terraform-142-your-team-wants-to-enforce-consistent-ta","sec":"terraform-s141","q":"In Python, how do you enforce consistent tags with Terraform and <code>boto3</code>?","a":"<p>Use <code>boto3</code> to audit resource tags and <code>python-terraform</code> to update the configuration with consistent tags.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0344","card":"q-terraform-142-your-team-wants-to-enforce-consistent-ta","sec":"terraform-s141","q":"In Python, in a script that adds missing tags to EC2 instances, how are the missing tags found and added?","a":"<p>It builds <code>current_tags</code>, computes <code>missing_tags</code> from <code>required_tags</code>, and calls <code>create_tags</code> when any are missing.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>            current_tags = {t[&quot;Key&quot;]: t[&quot;Value&quot;] for t in instance.get(&quot;Tags&quot;, [])}\n            missing_tags = {k: v for k, v in required_tags.items() if k not in current_tags}\n                ec2.create_tags(Resources=[instance_id], Tags=[{&quot;Key&quot;: k, &quot;Value&quot;: v} for k, v in missing_tags.items()])</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"terraform-f0345","card":"q-terraform-142-your-team-wants-to-enforce-consistent-ta","sec":"terraform-s141","q":"In Python, in a script that adds missing tags to EC2 instances, how are the tags passed to Terraform?","a":"<p>It calls <code>tf.apply(var={\"tags\": required_tags}, skip_plan=True)</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>    tf.apply(var={&quot;tags&quot;: required_tags}, skip_plan=True)</code></pre></div>","hand":true}];
